@prefix pmt:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/traditions/> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix pmp:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/practices/> .
@prefix pmw:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/works/> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .


#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V:
# Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006)
#
# The harvest of the fifth Stupen', kept apart from traditions/transerfing.ttl,
# which declares the tradition and its works. Read: chapters XVIII and XIX and
# the afterword of the combined edition (Ves, 2012), in its English
# translation; the text layer has no page numbers, every source names chapter
# and section heading. The afterword is absent from the Bulgarian translation
# of this Stupen', so every afterword source says that its place in the single
# volume is open. The glossary of the combined edition is not harvested: it
# restates the terms of all five Stupeni.
#
# Two independent passes over two parts with reconciliation, then one
# integrator per part reading the whole part (prima-materia#924). Parts:
# chapter XVIII; chapter XIX and afterword. Shared system terms are typed once,
# by the part that introduces them. The harvests of Stupen' I to IV are linked,
# not repeated.
#

#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V:
# Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), part 1: chapter XVIII The Mirror World.
#
# Two independent extraction passes ran over the text (A 127 records, B 91;
# 10 records of B without counterpart in A: 2 added, 6 covered, 2 not owed);
# a reader of the whole part added 3 records both passes missed (the fifth
# principle as the condition of outer intention, the correcting of the mind's
# scripts for the unforeseen, and the old idea turned into a technique) and
# settled 5 open questions: the order-and-release method ascribed to 'some
# people' is a practice with its condition of failure, not a dispute; Maker
# status 'as long as' one moves oneself is a prescribed order, the text naming
# no consequence; the mirror circle is ordered as a whole and becomes two
# series (closed and reversed) over three stations; Vanga's childhood games are
# a third-party case and their link to her clairvoyance the author's
# inference; the seven mirror principles are the author's systematization.
# The three Maker prerequisites of pass A are merged into one, prior step
# moving oneself.
#
# Stupen' I to IV (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl to -4.ttl) are not
# restated: 12 records whose claim a node there already carries are left
# out and linked; 32 nodes that restate an earlier node with a
# difference say so in a note.
#
# Shared system terms typed here: pmc:TranserfingDualMirrorCh18,
# pmc:TranserfingMirrorPrinciplesCh18, pmc:TranserfingAmalgamCh18. Part 2
# (chapter XIX) types pmc:TranserfingGatekeeperCh19,
# pmc:TranserfingRightOfTheMakerCh19 and pmc:TranserfingFrameOfIntentionCh19;
# of these only the Maker's right is mentioned here, in a note. The polemics
# against Vanga's fatalism, the mirror makers and the scientists are concepts,
# since only the author's side is read.
#

#
# ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'
#

pmc:TranserfingDualMirrorCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dual mirror"@en, "Doppelspiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The whole world is modelled as one immense two-faced mirror: the physical universe is the tangible face, the metaphysical alternatives space the other. Unlike a common mirror, matter here reflects the intention and thought of God and of the living beings who embody Him, and the alternatives space works as the pattern after which all matter is cut and moved."@en ;
    skos:note "Original term: dual'noe zerkalo (Bulgarian translation: Дуалното огледало, which is also the chapter title there)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTwoSidesOfRealityCh17: the two-faced reality of Stupen' IV is named here the dual mirror and becomes the frame of seven numbered mirror principles (pmc:TranserfingMirrorPrinciplesCh18). God as the source of the mirrored intention is linked to pmc:TranserfingGodRulesThroughAllBeingsCh17, not retyped."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAlternativesSpaceAsOrderCatalogueCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Alternatives space as order catalogue"@en, "Variantenraum als Bestellkatalog"@de ;
    skos:definition "On the far side of the mirror everything is held to exist in plenty and without rivalry; one picks what one wants as from a mail-order list, and the order is filled sooner or later free of charge if a few manageable conditions are kept. Radiated thought energy is said to materialise the sector whose quality matches it."@en ;
    skos:note "Contrasted with the picture of people jostling at near-empty shop counters, which is traced to a bleak outlook that then materialises."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLimitsOfInnerIntentionCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Limits of inner intention in the material world"@en, "Grenzen des inneren Intents in der stofflichen Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reduced to direct impact on matter, every living being moves only within inner intention: goals shrink to what is already at hand, means and chances are scarce and everything is contested. Because matter answers pushing at once, the illusion arises that pushing is the only route to results."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie: the limits are spelled out as scarcity of means, few opportunities and universal competition on the material face of the mirror."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoFactorsOfTheLayerCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two factors that form the layer of one's world"@en, "Zwei Faktoren, die die Schicht der eigenen Welt bilden"@de ;
    skos:definition "A person's layer of reality is built from both faces of the mirror: by direct action on objects on this side (inner intention) and by thought, which embodies on the far side what is not yet present (outer intention). Expectations of empty shelves, long queues and hostility are said to be confirmed, and so is the innocent assumption that the world has kept the best for oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingLayerOfOnesWorld: the layer is assigned here to the two sides of the dual mirror; birth conditions are granted weight, but the later course is said to depend largely on one's attitude to oneself and the world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFirstMirrorPrincipleCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "First mirror principle"@en, "Erstes Spiegelprinzip"@de ;
    skos:definition "The world acts as a mirror of one's relationship to it and literally consents to what one thinks of it."@en ;
    skos:note "Illustrated by the world's standing riddle, guess what I am like: each person answers from their own perception (cosy, hostile, ill-fated) and each answer wins, since the world then appears in the image ordered."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWorldMirrorRelationshipCh14: the mirroring is numbered here as the first of seven principles and extended from one's stance to one's thoughts about the world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSecondMirrorPrincipleCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Second mirror principle"@en, "Zweites Spiegelprinzip"@de ;
    skos:definition "A reflection forms only where heart and mind agree. In that agreement outer intention arises, the thought image takes sharp outlines and is embodied at once; where soul and intellect pull apart, the image blurs."@en ;
    skos:note "Given as the reason why fears come true while hopes do not."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma: heart-mind unity is numbered here as the second mirror principle and stated as the condition of any reflection."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOuterIntentionNeedsHeartMindUnityCh18 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Outer intention needs unity of heart and mind"@en, "Äußerer Intent setzt Einheit von Herz und Verstand voraus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention is said to emerge only while mind and heart do not oppose each other."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingHeartMindUnityBeforeControlOuterCh9: there unity suffices to bring outer intention under one's will; here it is the condition without which outer intention does not appear, and the consequence is named. The unity that fear and hatred produce unconditionally is carried by pmc:TranserfingAgreementInAversionCh7 and not repeated."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "When unity breaks, the image blurs and splits between what the heart wants and what the intellect insists on." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingOrderAndReleaseCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Order and release"@en, "Bestellen und Loslassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A method ascribed to unnamed others: state the order clearly, send the matching thought form out into the universe, then do nothing so as not to get in the way of its realisation."@en ;
    skos:note "Ascribed by the author to 'some people'; no person, school or tradition is named, and only the author's restriction of it is read, so it is recorded as a practice with its condition of failure (pmc:TranserfingOrderAndReleaseFailsWithoutUnityCh18), not as a dispute."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOrderAndReleaseFailsWithoutUnityCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Order and release fails without unity"@en, "Bestellen und Loslassen scheitert ohne Einheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The release method works only once the second mirror principle is met; since doubt can almost never be shed completely, that unity is rare and the method then does not work."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: the release method works only once the second mirror principle is met; since doubt can almost never be shed completely, that unity is rare and the method then does not work; it bears on pmp:TranserfingOrderAndReleaseCh18."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThirdMirrorPrincipleCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Third mirror principle"@en, "Drittes Spiegelprinzip"@de ;
    skos:definition "The dual mirror answers with a delay. As in an imagined looking-glass whose picture develops slowly like a photograph and shows raised arms only if they are held up for a while, material realisation is sluggish as tar, so the changes it makes are hardly noticeable. Where the second principle cannot be met, the goal is to be taken by long siege."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWorldMirrorRelationshipCh14: the lag of the world's answer, mentioned there in passing, is numbered here as a principle of its own and made the ground of the slide work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSlideSiegeYieldsMaterialisationCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Long slide work yields materialisation"@en, "Lange Diaarbeit bewirkt Materialisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Running the slide of the goal systematically over a long span is said to be the one basic condition under which a thought form materialises, the time needed growing with the complexity of the goal."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTargetSlideYieldsTransitionTargetLineX10: the slide's effect is grounded here in the delay of the dual mirror and called a siege, the ordinary daily effort that stands in for heart and mind not yet at one. This practice (pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10) and the capacity (pmc:TranserfingThoughtMaterialisesSector) are carried by Stupen' II and I and linked."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingThoughtMaterialisesSector ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSlideSiegeYieldsHeartMindUnityCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Long slide work yields unity of heart and mind"@en, "Lange Diaarbeit bewirkt Einheit von Herz und Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "As the first visible effects persuade the mind that the goal is reachable, heart and mind are said to come gradually into unity and focus the radiated image more sharply."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImpatienceShelvesTheSlideCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Impatience shelves the slide"@en, "Ungeduld legt das Dia beiseite"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most people lack the patience: kindled by an idea, they soon cool and put it aside for later; whoever skips the slide work is told not to expect a miracle."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: most people lack the patience: kindled by an idea, they soon cool and put it aside for later; whoever skips the slide work is told not to expect a miracle; it bears on pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingUnsystematicSlideBringsNoResultCh8: the failure is placed in fading enthusiasm before a mirror that answers late."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFirstImageInTheMirrorCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "First image appears in the mirror"@en, "Das erste Bild erscheint im Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "While the mind still doubts, the image stays hazy; sooner or later some outline of it shows, and one sees outer intention open the needed doors and supply the chances, which assures the mind that the technique bears fruit."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStagesOfSlideMaterialisationCh18 a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Stages of slide materialisation"@en, "Stufen der Materialisierung des Dias"@de ;
    skos:definition "The course of the siege as the text orders it: first a hazy image and the first visible traces with doors opening, then heart and mind come into unity, then the sharpened image is materialised and a dream once held impossible becomes real."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:TranserfingFirstImageInTheMirrorCh18 ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:TranserfingThoughtMaterialisesSector ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Heart and mind come into unity in the course of the siege, after the first evidence has convinced the mind, and materialisation follows it; the slide work does not wait for unity." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMirrorPrinciplesCh18 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seven mirror principles"@en, "Sieben Spiegelprinzipien"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author's numbered set of seven principles of the dual mirror, introduced one by one through the chapter and listed again in its summary: the world mirrors one's relationship to it; the reflection forms where heart and mind are one; the mirror answers late; it renders content and ignores orientation; attention goes from reflection to image; release the grip and let the world move with the flow; take every reflection as positive. The last is called the most important, and the last three together make up moving oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Members in order: pmc:TranserfingFirstMirrorPrincipleCh18, pmc:TranserfingSecondMirrorPrincipleCh18, pmc:TranserfingThirdMirrorPrincipleCh18, pmc:TranserfingFourthMirrorPrincipleCh18, pmc:TranserfingFifthMirrorPrincipleCh18, pmc:TranserfingSixthMirrorPrincipleCh18, pmc:TranserfingSeventhMirrorPrincipleCh18. The section given is where the first principle stands; principles four to seven follow in the next three sections."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Dual Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'
#

pmc:TranserfingAmalgamCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality amalgam"@en, "Amalgam der Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beyond any concrete slide, a steady background tone can be given to one's layer by choosing one dominant line among one's many relations to oneself and the world, as Venetian masters are said to have added gold to the backing of their mirrors so that warm tones prevailed in the reflection."@en ;
    skos:note "Original term: amal'gama. The chapter motto, that one's world cares for oneself, is the formula offered first."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAmalgamFormulaCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Working with the amalgam formula"@en, "Arbeit mit der Amalgamformel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: choose a dominant formula, for example that one's world takes care of oneself; bring one's outlook deliberately into line with it; confirm it in every circumstance, however small: when something lucky happens, note that the world cares for you, and when something disappoints, tell yourself that it unfolds as it should by the coordination of intention; at every problem declare that your world is to look after you; hand matters large and small to the world, e.g. on leaving without an umbrella under a threatening sky, do not turn back but declare a walk together with your world and ask it to look after you; aim intention at a world that protects you rather than at your own safety; keep stating the formula patiently at every opportunity until it is habit."@en ;
    skos:note "Alternative formulas offered: the world picks what is best for me, protects me, removes my problems, makes life easy, fulfils the order I place, knows better than I how to care for me; the reader may invent new ones or several."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFavourableLayerOfTheWorldCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Favourable layer of the world"@en, "Wohlwollende Schicht der Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "A cosy reality with a steady favourable background, in which one's world looks after one's welfare and its intention works on one's behalf."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAmalgamYieldsFavourableLayerCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Amalgam work yields a favourable layer"@en, "Amalgamarbeit bewirkt eine wohlwollende Schicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Controlling one's relationship to the world through the formula is said to make the dual mirror embody those sectors where one's world looks after one, a force stronger than one would expect."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAmalgamFormulaCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFavourableLayerOfTheWorldCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTrustInTheWorldCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Trust in the world"@en, "Vertrauen in die Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Relying on one's world to solve problems and protect, instead of the adult insistence on managing everything oneself; the author calls learning it essential, since the world's capacity to solve problems is said to be immeasurably greater than one's own."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAmalgamYieldsTrustInTheWorldCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Amalgam work yields trust in the world"@en, "Amalgamarbeit bewirkt Vertrauen in die Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Telling oneself at each problem that one lets the world take care of one is presented as the way to break the ice of mistrust."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAmalgamFormulaCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingTrustInTheWorldCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCascadeOfPleasantEventsCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cascade of pleasant events"@en, "Kaskade angenehmer Ereignisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: the layer changes visibly, surprisingly fast, a flood of pleasant events follows, and one feels a rising wind of change and never looks at the world mirror the same way again."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingAmalgamFormulaCh18."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPersistenceUntilHabitCh18 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Persistence until the formula is habit"@en, "Beharrlichkeit, bis die Formel Gewohnheit ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sustained effort is said to be needed only at the start, until stating the formula has become habit; from then on the favourable layer follows with ease."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingFavourableLayerOfTheWorldCh18 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingAmalgamFormulaCh18 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotHurryTheMirrorCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not hurry the mirror"@en, "Den Spiegel nicht drängen"@de ;
    skos:definition "By the third mirror principle the estranged world needs time to become its old self again; patience and self-control are needed at first, and one must not tire of stating the formula."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAmalgamFormulaCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSetbacksAreNoDisproofCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Setbacks are no disproof"@en, "Rückschläge sind kein Gegenbeweis"@de ;
    skos:definition "When things go wrong, do not take offence or doubt bitterly that the world cares, and do not battle with the doubts either, which is useless; leave room for errors and setbacks and keep the overall course."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAmalgamFormulaCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotMereOptimismCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not a call to optimism"@en, "Kein bloßer Aufruf zum Optimismus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking control of one's relationship to reality is not to be read as a vague appeal to see life more brightly but as concrete steps of shaping one's reality."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingConsciousControlOfOutlookCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRecallingChildhoodSerenityCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Recalling childhood serenity"@en, "Erinnern kindlicher Geborgenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: cast the mind back to moments of childhood when you felt safe and serene (a grandmother's kitchen, fishing on a river bank, sledging); notice that the world then took care of you; then look around now and see that it still does: flowers, sun, clouds, shelter from rain, rest after work; wake from the illusion that the past is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingConsciousControlOfOutlookCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Conscious control of one's outlook"@en, "Bewusste Lenkung der Lebenshaltung"@de ;
    skos:definition "From now on, come what may, adopt the rule of steering your attitude to life deliberately instead of reacting out of habit, oyster-like, only when dissatisfied; remind yourself that things are not that bad and could be much worse."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRenewedLayerOfTheWorldCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Renewed layer and childhood joy"@en, "Erneuerte Schicht und kindliche Lebensfreude"@de ;
    skos:definition "Regaining the calm serenity of childhood, the freshness of things, hope of better days and delight in living by renewing the layer of one's world."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOutlookControlRenewsTheLayerCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Outlook control renews the layer"@en, "Haltungslenkung erneuert die Schicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking control of one's relationship to reality is said to renew the layer of one's world: the world turns into whatever one's perception makes of it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingConsciousControlOfOutlookCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRenewedLayerOfTheWorldCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChildhoodRecallRestoresSerenityCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Childhood recall restores serenity"@en, "Kindheitserinnerung bringt Geborgenheit zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recalling the caring world of childhood and seeing that it is unchanged is offered as the way back to that serenity, which is said to be very easy and to need no belief, only a try."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRecallingChildhoodSerenityCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRenewedLayerOfTheWorldCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDissatisfactionDimsTheLayerCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Growing dissatisfaction dims the layer"@en, "Wachsende Unzufriedenheit verdunkelt die Schicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Life's colours are said to fade not because problems multiply with age but because one learns to voice negative attitudes: dissatisfaction outweighs contentment, the spoiled ward reproaches the world for not caring, the mirror consents, reality worsens, which gives new grounds for complaint, until the layer grows dull and uncomfortable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingViciousCircleOfDissatisfaction: the loop is told as the history of a cherished child turned grumbler; the world is said not to have changed, only one's relation to it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotSlightTheWorldCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not slight the world with ingratitude"@en, "Die Welt nicht durch Undank kränken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once reconciled with the world, one must never again offend this old and faithful servant by a thankless attitude."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAmalgamFormulaCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerIntentionCannotAvertAllThreatsCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Inner intention cannot avert all threats"@en, "Innerer Intent wendet nicht alle Gefahren ab"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since one's layer intersects countless other layers, no one can avoid every danger by inner intention; aim intention instead at creating a world that protects you, and its intention starts to work for you."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Reality Amalgam'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'Chasing Your Reflection'
#

pmc:TranserfingClosedFeedbackLoopOfReflectionCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Closed feedback loop of image and reflection"@en, "Geschlossene Rückkopplung von Bild und Spiegelbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reality is formed as a reflection of a person's thought forms, while those forms are shaped largely by the reflection. Fixed on the mirror, people let the reflection rather than the image lead the loop, and so they actively receive what they do not want."@en ;
    skos:note "The paradox is put as: one thinks about what one does not want and does not want what one thinks about."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'Chasing Your Reflection'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThoughtsAsOnesEnemyCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "One's thoughts as one's enemy"@en, "Die eigenen Gedanken als Feind"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mirror ignores willingness or reluctance and returns only the content of the image; hatred, curses and condemnation come back like a boomerang into one's own layer, as with the bitter old woman whose reproach of the world produces total injustice around her."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingClosedFeedbackLoopOfReflectionCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'Chasing Your Reflection'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAversionInstilsThoughtFormInAnothersLayerCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Aversion can instil its thought form in another's layer"@en, "Abneigung kann ihre Gedankenform in eine fremde Schicht tragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A woman who sharply rejects drinking is said to be fated to meet it everywhere, even to marry a drinker; the stronger her aversion, the more he drinks, and unless the husband has a firm intent of his own, her insistent aversion ends by implanting her thought form in the layer of his world."@en ;
    skos:note "Added in reconciliation: recorded by pass B only."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingIdealPartnerImage: beyond drawing a drinker into one's life, the aversion is said to carry over into the partner's layer, limited by his own firm intent. It stands beside pmc:TranserfingOnlyOnesOwnLayerCh18, by which no one steers another's life by intention; the text does not reconcile the two."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'Chasing Your Reflection'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNegativeSelfRelationIsMirroredCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pessimism, grudges and self-dislike are mirrored"@en, "Pessimismus, Groll und Selbstablehnung werden gespiegelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pessimism, likened to a kind of sadomasochism, the habit of nursing grudges, whining, self-dislike, low self-esteem and guilt are each confirmed by the mirror: the embittered person orders a failure script, the self-doubter is told he is mediocre, and whoever feels guilty, even unconsciously, will surely see some retribution reflected."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPunishmentScript: guilt is set in a row with pessimism and self-dislike, all read as orders the mirror merely fills."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingFirstMirrorPrincipleCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'Chasing Your Reflection'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfAdmirationPrincipleCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Principle of self-admiration"@en, "Prinzip der Selbstbewunderung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most small children are attractive; those who grow up beautiful are held to be those who admire themselves, since liking oneself gives ever more reason to like oneself. Remarks to the reflection about weight or a puny build are echoed back as verdicts, which is how inferiority complexes form."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingDwellingOnFlaws: the self-image is given as a tautology the mirror reinforces in both directions, toward beauty as well as toward complexes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'Chasing Your Reflection'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFearDoubtAndAvoidanceMirroredCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear, doubt and avoidance in the mirror"@en, "Angst, Zweifel und Vermeidung im Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fear draws an unfortunate event when it lies near the alternatives flow, while most feared things never happen because they would cost too much energy; doubt, fixed on what will not happen, is confirmed in its turn; the wish to avoid something raises its likelihood and leaves one irritated most of the time, an overall image of discomfort that reality then keeps up."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAvoidanceAttracts: doubt is set beside fear as the mirror of what does not happen, and the resulting irritation is read as one integrated image. That misfortune is an anomaly of the flow is carried by pmc:TranserfingMisfortuneIsAnomaly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'Chasing Your Reflection'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFourthMirrorPrincipleCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fourth mirror principle"@en, "Viertes Spiegelprinzip"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mirror renders the content of a relationship and disregards its direction: any attitude fed by the heart's passion and the mind's conviction is reproduced exactly, whether it expresses attraction or aversion."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingFixation: the indifference of the result to love or hate is numbered here as the fourth mirror principle."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'Chasing Your Reflection'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChasingTheReflectionCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Chasing the reflection"@en, "Dem Spiegelbild nachjagen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trying to change unwanted results by acting directly on the reflection, the reality already realised, is absurd and often impossible, like rebuilding a finished house; once an obstacle has captured one's attention, collision follows, as in a skid where braking speeds the slide, and reality rules the person."@en ;
    skos:note "The author tells, in the first person, of running and shouting as a child so that the world would listen, and owns that as an adult he still behaves so; it illustrates the chase."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingManipulatingTheReflectionCh17: the futile grip on the reflection is drawn as a chase in which inner intention blows in one's face."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingVnutrenneeNamerenie ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'Chasing Your Reflection'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHaltingTheChaseCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Halting the chase"@en, "Anhalten der Jagd"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: stop pursuing your own reflection and pause; draw your gaze away from the mirror; release inner intention's effort to push the world where you want it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'Chasing Your Reflection'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheWorldComesToMeetOneCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The world comes to meet one"@en, "Die Welt kommt einem entgegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state in which reality, once halted, moves toward the person of its own accord, carried by outer intention instead of one's effort; the wind in one's face is now that of outer intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingWorldMirrorRelationshipCh14: the approach of the world follows here from halting the chase after the reflection."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'Chasing Your Reflection'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHaltingTheChaseBringsTheWorldCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Halting the chase brings the world closer"@en, "Anhalten der Jagd bringt die Welt entgegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ending the chase is said to stop the runaway car of reality in its tracks, after which the world comes to meet one."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingHaltingTheChaseCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingTheWorldComesToMeetOneCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'Chasing Your Reflection'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'
#

pmc:TranserfingThreadsOfImportanceToTheMirrorCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Threads of importance binding one to the mirror"@en, "Fäden der Bedeutsamkeit, die an den Spiegel binden"@de ;
    skos:definition "People are tied to the mirror by importance, since what it shows is their life. The stronger the feeling, liked or disliked, the tighter the tie; only what one thinks about counts, not what one thinks of it, so the reflection keeps strengthening the existing state: the poor get poorer, the rich richer, and one should say not 'this is how we live' but that we live as we think about our existence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStartingConditionsDoNotFixLifeCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Starting conditions do not fix one's life"@en, "Startbedingungen legen das Leben nicht fest"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against the stock objection that some are born poor and some rich: the start positions the image of a life and counts for much, but rises from poverty and falls from wealth show the rule is not fixed; whatever hole one is in, everything can be changed radically, and the way out need not be seen beforehand, since the solution will show itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingObservingRealityCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Observing reality (station of the mirror circle)"@en, "Wirklichkeit beobachten (Station des Spiegelkreises)"@de ;
    skos:definition "One of the three stations of the mirror circle: looking at what the mirror currently shows, the reality already realised."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingExpressingTheAttitudeCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Expressing one's attitude (station of the mirror circle)"@en, "Die eigene Haltung äußern (Station des Spiegelkreises)"@de ;
    skos:definition "One of the three stations of the mirror circle: stating one's relationship, either as a reaction to what was seen or as a deliberate image of what one wants to see."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMirrorConsolidatesTheAttitudeCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mirror consolidates the attitude (station of the mirror circle)"@en, "Der Spiegel verfestigt die Haltung (Station des Spiegelkreises)"@de ;
    skos:definition "One of the three stations of the mirror circle: the mirror fixes the content of the expressed attitude as reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingClosedMirrorCircleCh18 a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Closed mirror circle"@en, "Geschlossener Spiegelkreis"@de ;
    skos:definition "The circle in which people are said to walk unawares: observe reality, express an attitude to it, and the mirror consolidates that attitude's content in reality, like a donkey after a carrot dangled before it."@en ;
    skos:note "The text says reality is changed only by breaking this circle."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:TranserfingObservingRealityCh18 ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:TranserfingExpressingTheAttitudeCh18 ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:TranserfingMirrorConsolidatesTheAttitudeCh18 ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Because observing comes first, the attitude is a reaction to the reflection, so the mirror keeps confirming what is already there." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReversedMirrorCircleCh18 a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Reversed mirror circle"@en, "Umgekehrter Spiegelkreis"@de ;
    skos:definition "The same three stations in the order the text prescribes: express a deliberate attitude first, let the mirror consolidate its content in reality, and observe only at the end; the circle then spins by itself, driven by outer intention."@en ;
    skos:note "The author admits the order looks strange, since people are used to voicing what they see; the mirror is imagined asking what one does want."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:TranserfingExpressingTheAttitudeCh18 ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:TranserfingMirrorConsolidatesTheAttitudeCh18 ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:TranserfingObservingRealityCh18 ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Putting the statement of the image before observation replaces a reaction to the reflection with an intended image, and outer intention takes the place of inner intention." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFifthMirrorPrincipleCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fifth mirror principle"@en, "Fünftes Spiegelprinzip"@de ;
    skos:definition "To launch outer intention, attention has to shift off the reflection onto the image: one takes control of one's thoughts and thinks of what one wants and strives for, not of what one does not want or seeks to avoid."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFifthPrincipleBeforeOuterIntentionCh18 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Fifth principle before outer intention"@en, "Fünftes Prinzip vor dem äußeren Intent"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mechanism of outer intention is said to start only once the fifth mirror principle is met; inner intention aimed at the reflection has too few opportunities on this side of the mirror."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes. No consequence of skipping beyond the weakness of inner intention is quoted, so the strength is prescribedOrder."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingFifthMirrorPrincipleCh18 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingThoughtInventoryCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Thought inventory and the wanted image"@en, "Gedankeninventur und das gewünschte Bild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: take stock of your thoughts and strike out every 'not'; throw dissatisfaction, reluctance, disapproval, hate and disbelief in success into the rubbish sack; tune thinking to what you want and like; no longer react to your life's reality but send chosen thought forms out on purpose, holding a positive attitude against the visible negative reflection; keep the outlook of someone who already has the goal or is about to receive it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDeliberateMoodCreationCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Deliberate creation of mood"@en, "Bewusstes Erzeugen der Stimmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: whatever the circumstances, do consciously what lifts your spirits instead of reacting to irritants; use visual or musical slides, ideally a picture of the goal attained and of yourself feeling splendid; make this a habit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCommandOverOnesRealityCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Command over one's reality"@en, "Herrschaft über die eigene Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choosing the colours of one's reality by intention and deciding one's own fate instead of being a victim of circumstance; whoever manages their thinking manages their reality, and whoever cannot is managed by it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThoughtInventoryYieldsCommandOverRealityCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Thought inventory yields command over reality"@en, "Gedankeninventur bewirkt Herrschaft über die Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Replacing negative attitudes by the images one wants is said to make only pleasant things show in the mirror."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingThoughtInventoryCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCommandOverOnesRealityCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMoodCreationYieldsCommandOverRealityCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Mood creation yields command over reality"@en, "Stimmungsarbeit bewirkt Herrschaft über die Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Consciously set mood is presented as the means by which one chooses the colours of one's reality; even knowing that one can shape reality is said to raise the spirits."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDeliberateMoodCreationCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCommandOverOnesRealityCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLullAndSurfacingProblemsCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Lull and surfacing problems"@en, "Flaute und auftauchende Probleme"@de ;
    skos:definition "A favourable reality does not come at once: expect a stretch with no visible change, or problems creeping out as if to spite you, which are passing troubles of moving to a new relationship with reality; stand firm, hold the pause and do not look back, as in the tale where turning round turns one to stone."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingThoughtInventoryCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingGlancingIntoTheWorldMirrorCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Only glancing into the world mirror"@en, "Nur flüchtig in den Weltspiegel blicken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: make it a rule not to stare at the world mirror but only to peep; pass over the negative and look for the good, letting all perception pass through that filter; with your own looks, search only for the traits you want while picturing your desired image; seek steady confirmation that things improve day by day; form the relationship first and glance in the mirror after, never the reverse."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingFilteringNews: the filter is turned on one's own reflection and tied to the rule of forming the relationship before looking."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDesiredSelfImageCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Desired self-image"@en, "Gewünschtes Selbstbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "A reflection of oneself, one's appearance included, transformed toward the wanted image, since the world mirror shows one's relationship to oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGlancingYieldsDesiredSelfImageCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Glancing yields the desired self-image"@en, "Flüchtiges Blicken bewirkt das gewünschte Selbstbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Practised regularly, the technique is said to turn the reflection gradually positive despite the inertia of material realisation."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingGlancingIntoTheWorldMirrorCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingDesiredSelfImageCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAstonishmentAtQuickChangeCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Astonishment at quick change"@en, "Staunen über raschen Wandel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: whoever practises regularly will soon be open-mouthed with surprise as things get better every day."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingGlancingIntoTheWorldMirrorCh18."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheCircleSpinsByItselfCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The circle spins by itself"@en, "Der Kreis dreht sich von selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: the layer fills with so much that is good that one no longer has to talk oneself into enjoyment; once set going and speeded up by intention, the mirror circle turns lightly of its own accord."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingThoughtInventoryCh18."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBeliefNotRequiredCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Belief is not required"@en, "Glaube ist nicht erforderlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "No belief is needed, only practice and seeing the consequences; outer intention works discreetly, and the mind will not accept it until it faces a realised fact, so let the mind potter about in doubt while you do the work."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingThoughtInventoryCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTooSimpleToTryCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Too simple to be tried"@en, "Zu einfach, um es zu versuchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first reason for missing results: the technique seems too simple and the effect of thought on reality hard to believe, so people do not take it seriously and never try."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: the first reason for missing results: the technique seems too simple and the effect of thought on reality hard to believe, so people do not take it seriously and never try; it bears on pmp:TranserfingThoughtInventoryCh18."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLackOfMethodicalActionCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lack of methodical action"@en, "Fehlendes methodisches Handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "The second reason: no methodical work; inspiration flares and dies as quickly, and a mirror that answers late cannot form a reflection for someone who stands before it a moment and runs off; the work is done with the head, not the hands."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: the second reason: no methodical work; inspiration flares and dies as quickly, and a mirror that answers late cannot form a reflection for someone who stands before it a moment and runs off; the work is done with the head, not the hands; it bears on pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotSuppressingEmotionsCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not by suppressing emotions"@en, "Nicht durch Unterdrücken der Gefühle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Freedom from the mirror is not won by suppressing emotions, which only follow from the relationship; what must change is its essence, the way one perceives and answers reality."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingThoughtInventoryCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromTheMirrorCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from the mirror"@en, "Freiheit vom Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Release from the feelings that tie one to the reflection, which brings the ability to create the kind of reflection one wishes to see."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThoughtInventoryYieldsFreedomFromTheMirrorCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Changing the relationship yields freedom from the mirror"@en, "Veränderte Beziehung bewirkt Freiheit vom Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mastering the feelings that bind one to the reflection, by changing the relationship, is said to free one from the mirror."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingThoughtInventoryCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromTheMirrorCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGradedIntensityOfMirrorWorkCh18 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Graded intensity of mirror work"@en, "Abgestufte Intensität der Spiegelarbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author ranks the ways of taking control of reality by effort: the amalgam as simplest, giving an overall backdrop of comfort and wellbeing that mostly suffices; realising a particular dream as more demanding, needing more patience and focus; each person uses the technique as far as their needs require."@en ;
    skos:note "Amalgam: pmc:TranserfingAmalgamCh18 with pmp:TranserfingAmalgamFormulaCh18; dream: pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOldIdeaMadeIntoTechniqueCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "An old idea turned into a technique"@en, "Eine alte Idee als Technik"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author grants that the world as a reflection of our thoughts is no new idea: it is understood implicitly by many but stays vague, so it brings little practical gain; few have time for spiritual enlightenment or the secrets of natural forces, and what he claims to add is a specific technique with an account of how it works."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes. No earlier holder of the idea is named."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The World Comes To You'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'
#

pmc:TranserfingMagicAsKnowledgeOfTheDualMirrorCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic as knowledge of the dual mirror"@en, "Magie als Kenntnis des Doppelspiegels"@de ;
    skos:definition "There is said to be no magic as such, only knowledge of the dual mirror's principles, so plain and accessible that it never fits the canons of the magical, as Aladdin's lamp resembled a battered tin and the Grail was no golden cup. What is great is simple; emptiness hides behind mystery. Brought into everyday life, magic loses its mystery, and everyday reality turns into an unknown, controllable waking dream for whoever keeps the principles."@en ;
    skos:note "Called genuine magic without its trappings yet with real force, in the passage on holding the pause."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReadingTheDelayAsFailureCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reading the delay as failure"@en, "Die Verzögerung als Misserfolg deuten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seeing no visible result, the restless mind judges the action wrong or useless; the mirror reflects exactly that judgement, and the process slows down or changes direction."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: seeing no visible result, the restless mind judges the action wrong or useless; the mirror reflects exactly that judgement, and the process slows down or changes direction; it bears on pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10."@en ;
    skos:note "Illustrated by a dialogue in which the mind, like a child promised a toy, demands it this minute and then doubts the route the mirror takes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingClingingToOnesOwnScriptCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Clinging to one's own script"@en, "Am eigenen Drehbuch festhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once the goal image is set, only the mirror knows the route; when events take an unforeseen course the mind raises the alarm, grabs the world by the throat, warps the target slide and acts for the scenario it prefers, blocking the route it cannot grasp that would have led to success."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: once the goal image is set, only the mirror knows the route; when events take an unforeseen course the mind raises the alarm, grabs the world by the throat, warps the target slide and acts for the scenario it prefers, blocking the route it cannot grasp that would have led to success; it bears on pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMindAsCyberneticMachineCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mind as a cybernetic machine"@en, "Der Verstand als kybernetische Maschine"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind behaves like a machine whose red lamp lights when its algorithm is disturbed, except that it writes its own programs, naively assumes it can foresee every variable, chooses a stereotyped plan and insists on it; any unforeseen deviation is met with hostility and a grab at the reflection, the trap of a kitten playing with its double in a mirror."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThreefoldDistortedMirrorCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Threefold distorted mirror"@en, "Dreifach verzerrter Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Desire is needed for striving; desire with resolve to act is will; desire with doubt and fear of failure is longing, an importance to be lowered on purpose. Taking on the burden of success or failure, one places harsh demands on oneself and the world, and the mirror is distorted three ways: I want, I fear, I cannot let go."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImpatientLongingDistortsTheMirrorCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Impatient longing distorts the mirror"@en, "Ungeduldiges Verlangen verzerrt den Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The urge to have the result as soon as possible, mixed with doubt and fear, builds excess potential to the point where the mirror warps and the order is not realised."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: the urge to have the result as soon as possible, mixed with doubt and fear, builds excess potential to the point where the mirror warps and the order is not realised; it bears on pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingBurningDesireDelaysTheOrderCh12: the delay is read here as a warping of the dual mirror by excess potential (pmc:TranserfingIzbytochnyPotentsial, linked)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotDemandOrPleadCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not demand or plead"@en, "Nicht fordern, nicht bitten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking intention as a firm demand for what the world owes, or as a request, leaves one empty-handed, since the world mirrors the demands, requests, fears and doubts back; one only places the order and lets the world carry it out."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAllowingTheWorldCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAllowingTheWorldCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Allowing the world"@en, "Der Welt erlauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: let the world go and permit it to be cosy for you at this very moment; catch that subtle, fleeting feeling before it passes; imagine for a moment the hostile, troublesome world turned joyful and comfortable; do not force yourself to be happy but allow yourself the luxury of happiness and the idea of improbable luck; leave the means to the world, as one does not wonder how an ordinary mirror forms its picture."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingAllowingOneselfToHaveCh13: the permission is addressed to the world being comfortable now and to luck, not to deserving the goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAllowedHappinessCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Allowed happiness"@en, "Erlaubtes Glück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Happiness that enters life by one's permission rather than by default; one is said to be only as happy as one lets oneself conceive of incredible luck."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAllowingYieldsHappinessCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Allowing yields happiness"@en, "Erlauben bewirkt Glück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Granting oneself the luxury of happiness is presented as what lets happiness into life."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAllowingTheWorldCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAllowedHappinessCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHoldingTheImageThroughThePauseCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Holding the image through the pause"@en, "Das Bild durch die Pause halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps, for one whose regular slide work is under way: when the fidgety mind doubts because nothing or the unexpected happens, activate conscious awareness; recall the rule that turning round turns one to stone; keep attention on the final goal as though it had been reached already; remind yourself that the mirror needs a pause to assemble the reflection; through that pause stand firm and believe in success even when all seems lost; look into the mirror only to note positive shifts and enjoy surprise, eyes open to signs of the world moving toward the goal and shut to the inevitable negative side effects."@en ;
    skos:note "Given as the fifth principle recalled as instructions, for readers who find it easier to follow a set of steps."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTurningBackToTheReflectionCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Turning back to the reflection"@en, "Sich zum Spiegelbild umdrehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "As soon as one turns to the reflection, whatever it shows or fails to show, the world halts and one is back on the tiring, futile lap round the mirror circle."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: as soon as one turns to the reflection, whatever it shows or fails to show, the world halts and one is back on the tiring, futile lap round the mirror circle; it bears on pmp:TranserfingHoldingTheImageThroughThePauseCh18."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingResultsBeyondExpectationCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Results beyond expectation"@en, "Ergebnisse über Erwarten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: for whoever persists in never turning round, results as a rule exceed one's highest hopes; one gets not only the toy but the merry-go-round and an ice-cream besides."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingHoldingTheImageThroughThePauseCh18."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHoldingTheImageYieldsMaterialisationCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Holding the image yields materialisation"@en, "Das Bild halten bewirkt Materialisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "While one stays focused on the image, the world is said to come to one and the image to be materialised into physical reality; what one receives depends on one's courage not to despond."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingHoldingTheImageThroughThePauseCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingThoughtMaterialisesSector ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMovingOneselfCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Moving oneself"@en, "Sich selbst bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The general rule for the mirror: move not the reflection but the image, that is, one's relationship and the focus of one's thoughts. Inner intention tries to act on the reflection; outer intention leaves the mirror alone and works on thought forms, a power able to move the world, which turns after one with some delay if one does not grab it."@en ;
    skos:note "Moving oneself is equated later with following the last three mirror principles."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingManipulatingTheReflectionCh17: the change of image is named here the rule of moving oneself and illustrated by a kitten playing with its double."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


pmp:TranserfingCorrectingTheMindsScriptsCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Correcting the mind's scripts for the unforeseen"@en, "Die Drehbücher des Verstandes für das Unvorhergesehene öffnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To free oneself from the illusion of grasping at the reflection, turn the mind's short-sighted intention round and have it revise its scripts on the move so that they make room for the unpredictable; keep the hands away from the mirror, be mild and flexible, and let the alternatives flow carry events on their best course."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes. The text calls this new task for the mind the sole exit from the role of the kitten."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSixthMirrorPrincipleCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sixth mirror principle"@en, "Sechstes Spiegelprinzip"@de ;
    skos:definition "Loosen the grip and let the world go along with the flow of alternatives; inner intention then reverses its course, and giving up the controlling position brings real command of the situation."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingControlByReleasingControl, which carries the paradox and the capacity: it is numbered here as the sixth mirror principle and tied to the turning of inner intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingObserverStanceWithTheFlowCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Observer stance with the flow"@en, "Beobachterhaltung im Fluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: watch everything around you as an observer who is part of the play yet detached; do not turn down an offer hastily; weigh advice; do not rush into debate over a different view; let go when someone seems to do something wrong; embrace changed circumstances instead of sounding the alarm; take the simplest course and the most natural option; move with the flow consciously, sensing when to tighten the reins and when to give slack, like a wise mentor who leaves the pupil free and only now and then gives a push."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingFollowingTheFlow: the steps are given as the working of the sixth mirror principle. That conscious movement with the current is not blind drifting is carried by pmc:TranserfingNeitherResistNorSurrender and not repeated."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingObserverStanceYieldsControlCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Observer stance yields real control"@en, "Beobachterhaltung bewirkt echte Kontrolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Letting the world go and watching how it moves is said to make the world begin to spin around one."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingObserverStanceWithTheFlowCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingControlByReleasingControl ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSeventhMirrorPrincipleCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seventh mirror principle"@en, "Siebtes Spiegelprinzip"@de ;
    skos:definition "Embrace every reflection as positive. Besides reflecting flawlessly the mirror inverts, as right becomes left, and people are inclined to find harm in what is good; since every event carries both a harmful and a favourable potential, the attitude one declares at that crossroads decides how events unfold, and when things go well one should rejoice and sharpen awareness of it."@en ;
    skos:note "Called the last, most important and most powerful of the mirror principles."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingKoordinatsiyaNamereniya: the text identifies the two, but grounds the principle in the inverting property of the mirror and numbers it seventh. That the alternatives flow follows least resistance is carried by pmc:TranserfingOptimalityPrinciple and not repeated."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDeclaringTheProblemSimpleCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Declaring the problem simple"@en, "Das Problem für einfach erklären"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: on meeting a problem, see yourself at a crossroads where you alone decide whether to call it complex or plain; declare it plain and being solved easily, even without feeling so, and hold this as a postulate; answer the question whether all is going to pot with the claim that everything is going great; rub or clap your hands or hop with pleasure, however foolish it looks; whenever any problem arises, remember that the world will comply with your relation to it."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingReversingTheAttitude: the reversal is aimed at declaring the problem simple, on the ground that only the accompanying circumstances make a problem complex and these follow one's relation to it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTurningSetbacksIntoAdvantageCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Turning setbacks into advantage"@en, "Rückschläge in Vorteile verwandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mastery of one's success: by will one declares any event favourable, and circumstances that seemed harmful turn out to be trump cards; held to differ from relying on the world's love, from confidence circumstances can shake, from blind faith and from an optimistic temperament."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDeclaringSimpleYieldsAdvantageCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Declaring the problem simple yields advantage"@en, "Einfach-Erklären bewirkt Vorteil"@de ;
    skos:definition "The declared positive relation to a problem is said soon to reveal the seemingly harmful circumstances as assets."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDeclaringTheProblemSimpleCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingTurningSetbacksIntoAdvantageCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDefeatTurnsToVictoryCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Defeat turns to victory"@en, "Niederlage wird Sieg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced in advance: whenever a defeat becomes a win one feels an incomparable delight, as at a magic trick, and the effect stays so sudden that one never gets used to it."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingDeclaringTheProblemSimpleCh18."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIntentionOfTheMakerCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intention of the Maker"@en, "Intention des Schöpfers"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being the maker of one's own reality and of the layer of one's world: a will that does not subordinate but allows, more observer than active agent, distinct from confidence, blind faith or optimism; with it one need not fear what others call hostile, problematic or intractable."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Original term: namerenie Sozdatelya. The chapter's last section speaks of the Maker's right; that term is typed in part 2 as pmc:TranserfingRightOfTheMakerCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMovingOneselfBeforeTheMakerCh18 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Moving oneself before being the Maker"@en, "Sich selbst bewegen, bevor man Schöpfer ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "One is the Maker of one's reality only as long as one knows how to move oneself without denying the world its freedom to move, which means following the last three mirror principles."@en ;
    skos:note "Stated as a standing condition ('as long as'); the text names no consequence of not keeping it, so the strength is prescribedOrder. The three principles are pmc:TranserfingFifthMirrorPrincipleCh18, pmc:TranserfingSixthMirrorPrincipleCh18 and pmc:TranserfingSeventhMirrorPrincipleCh18."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingIntentionOfTheMakerCh18 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingMovingOneselfCh18 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The Maker’s Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'
#

pmc:TranserfingFateAsChoiceInAMirrorWorldCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fate as choice in a mirror world"@en, "Schicksal als Wahl in einer Spiegelwelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Of the views that fate lies in its owner's hands, that it is predetermined, or that it is a lot earned in past lives, all are said to be right, since in a mirror world each holder is confirmed: a fixed script runs for one who believes in it, karma comes to one who wants it, while one who takes the oars can row the little boat of life away from its supposed fate."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingChosenWorldviewManifests: the views of fate are declared equally well founded, and the question of fate is reduced to the choice between a predestined and a free one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUncreatedAlternativesSpaceCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Uncreated alternatives space"@en, "Ungeschaffener Variantenraum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked who put its contents into the alternatives space and what came before it, the author says he does not know and offers only a hypothesis: no one made it, it has always existed; the mind's assumption that everything has a maker, a beginning and an end may not hold for everything, as a dot on a coordinate plane cannot conceive who drew the grid."@en ;
    skos:note "Added in reconciliation: recorded by pass B only. The author marks it as a hypothesis and admits not knowing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPredictionsBecomeIntentionCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Predictions become intention"@en, "Vorhersagen werden zur Intention"@de ;
    skos:definition "Forecasting is held possible because sectors of the alternatives space form causal chains, the life lines readable by signs such as the stars, dreams, cards or coffee grounds; yet among infinite alternatives a forecast is only probable and often wrong. Its relatively high hit rate is explained by the prediction lodging in memory: held half in jest, half seriously and with little importance, it creates a fleeting unity of heart and mind and a sharp image, which the mirror realises and the person unknowingly enacts."@en ;
    skos:note "Coincidence is declared not to exist: it is only an effect perceived without detailed knowledge of its cause."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingAstrologyNotNegated: the hit rate is traced to the forecast turning into the client's own intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVangaCh18 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Vanga"@en, "Wanga"@de ;
    skos:definition "Vangelia Dimitrova, the Bulgarian clairvoyant known worldwide as Vanga, said to have gained the gift to see into the alternatives space after losing her sight young, with hits about past and future between seventy and eighty percent; her foretelling that Kursk would sink, read only once the submarine of that name went down, is cited."@en ;
    skos:note "Her biography as the author reports it: at twelve she was carried off by a hurricane and found in a field covered with sand, and lost her sight in that accident."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Vangelia Dimitrova, known as Vanga" ;
    pm:nameRole "clairvoyant seeing the alternatives space" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNostradamusCh18 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Nostradamus"@en, "Nostradamus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Author of The Centuries, cited as an instance of prophecy that the seer's perception and later readers' interpretations distort, his text still receiving wildly diverging readings."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Nostradamus" ;
    pm:nameRole "prophet whose Centuries receive divergent readings" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSeeingTheAlternativesSpaceCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing the alternatives space"@en, "Schau des Variantenraums"@de ;
    skos:definition "Clairvoyant access to fragments of past and future held in the alternatives space, an archive of films of both; held real but bounded by probability, since nothing assures that the reel taken from the shelf will be the one projected, and open to distortion by the seer's perception and interpretation."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingClairvoyance: the limit is quantified by Vanga's hit rate (pmc:TranserfingVangaCh18)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingVangasChildhoodGamesCh18 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Vanga's childhood games"@en, "Wangas Kinderspiele"@de ;
    skos:definition "As reported of Vanga's childhood: she played at healing the neighbours' children as her patients, told invented stories that held her listeners spellbound, and hid a thing somewhere out of sight and then, eyes bound, groped her way to it."@en ;
    skos:note "A third-party case taken from her biography, not a prescribed exercise; the author reads it as unintended self-programming of her later fate (pmc:TranserfingVangasGamesYieldSeeingCh18)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVangasGamesYieldSeeingCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Vanga's childhood games yield clairvoyance"@en, "Wangas Kinderspiele bewirken Hellsicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author holds that the images of these games were so precise that the world mirror recreated them in physical reality, so that Vanga became healer and seer."@en ;
    skos:note "The games are a third-party case reported from her biography; the link to her clairvoyance is the author's own inference, which is why this node is attested as his text. He says only that her biography gives the impression of an intentional programming."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingVangasChildhoodGamesCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSeeingTheAlternativesSpaceCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstVangasFatalismCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against Vanga's fatalism"@en, "Gegen Wangas Fatalismus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Vanga is reported to have held fate inescapable and never to have averted the accidents she foresaw, since those warned did not believe her. The author denies that this contradicts Transurfing: no one can shape another's life by their own intention, and each manages their own fate only on taking the wheel themselves."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute in form, but only the author's side is read; Vanga's own view is known only as he reports it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOnlyOnesOwnLayerCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Only one's own layer"@en, "Nur die eigene Schicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "No one can influence another person's life by their own intention; each is given power over the layer of their own world only, and even a politician who seems to dispose of nations only executes what the structure that produced him wills."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingLayerOfOnesWorld ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGenuinePowerOverFateCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Genuine power over one's fate"@en, "Echte Macht über das eigene Schicksal"@de ;
    skos:definition "The active position, not thrashing in the water or rowing against the current and steering one's thoughts by the mirror principles, said to give real power over one's fate, turning life into a lucid dream one controls and making the services of seers unnecessary."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingControlOfDestiny: the power over fate is tied here to the active position and the mirror principles and set against consulting seers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMirrorThoughtControlYieldsPowerOverFateCh18 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Thought control by the principles yields power over fate"@en, "Gedankenlenkung nach den Prinzipien bewirkt Macht über das Schicksal"@de ;
    skos:definition "The intention to control one's thoughts according to the mirror principles is named as the active position that confers genuine power over one's fate."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingThoughtInventoryCh18 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingGenuinePowerOverFateCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMirrorMakersCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Mirror makers"@en, "Spiegelmacher"@de ;
    skos:definition "Astrologers, hierophants and prophesiers are cast as mirror makers: a forecast is no innocent forecast but an ersatz fragment of the client's fate, a small mirror one will have to look into; once heard, taken seriously or not, its image keeps programming the subconscious. The author grants that single predictions often come true and can warn or give hope, so the mirror makers serve those who choose life as unconscious dreaming, but one who would make life a controllable lucid dream needs none of them."@en ;
    skos:note "Original term: zerkal'shchiki. A dispute in form, but only the author's side is read."@en ;
    skos:note "Consulting them is also called a choice and a safe way of drifting along the stream of fate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPredictionAsCostlyPurchaseCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A prediction is a costly purchase"@en, "Eine Vorhersage ist ein teurer Kauf"@de ;
    skos:definition "A peek into the Book of Fate always costs the same: one must carry what was heard into one's life whether one wants to or not, which can prove fatal; the responsibility lies with the buyer, not the seller."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingMirrorMakersCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGlobalDoomForecastsCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Forecasts of global doom"@en, "Prognosen globalen Untergangs"@de ;
    skos:definition "The most harmful mirror makers are those who foretell catastrophe on a global scale and doomsday: they tune large groups to destructive thinking and so programme the collective consciousness, which will leave its mark."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingMirrorMakersCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAddictionToFateTradingPendulumsCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Addiction to pendulums that trade in fate"@en, "Sucht nach Pendeln, die mit Schicksal handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mirror makers' pendulums care nothing for the client's fate but for a steady energy supply; caught in the noose of such a pendulum, one cannot feel sure without the next horoscope or dream reading, and keeps taking the dose like a drug to prop up an illusory confidence in tomorrow."@en ;
    skos:note "The pendulum itself is carried by pmc:TranserfingMayatnik and pmc:TranserfingPendulumsCh16 and not retyped."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingMirrorMakersCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingScientistsAsMirrorMakersCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Scientists as mirror makers"@en, "Wissenschaftler als Spiegelmacher"@de ;
    skos:definition "Scientists are counted in the league too: from a flat earth on whales and a turtle, through the earth-centred sky, classical and quantum physics, particles that turn out waves, strings in ten dimensions and an eleventh added for membrane theory, the world agrees to each model; like a mirror holding a mirror the models are endless, and the world may look like nothing at all, two facing mirrors reflecting nothing into a black infinity, being only a mirror of our ideas."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingTwoSidesOfRealityCh17: the agreement of the world with every model is told as an endless regress of mirrors, and science is put among the mirror makers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTransurfingAsUtilitarianModelCh18 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transurfing as a utilitarian model"@en, "Transerfing als Nutzmodell"@de ;
    skos:definition "Transurfing claims not to account for the workings of the world but to offer a working model of why and how reality can be controlled, as one drives a car without knowing how the engine was built; its mission is to issue the driving licence."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingModelJudgedByResults: usefulness is set against the mirror makers' claim to describe the world, and the model's task is named as licensing the driver."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKnowledgeBecomesPendulumOnlyWithStructureCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Knowledge becomes a pendulum only with a structure"@en, "Wissen wird erst mit einer Struktur zum Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Transurfing is said to need no energy supply from its readers, and knowledge in itself is no pendulum; a pendulum arises only once a matching structure has formed, so the reader is to learn the principles and do with them as he likes."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingMethodAsPendulum: the line is drawn between the knowledge and a structure built on it, a self-qualification of the method."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingTransurfingAsUtilitarianModelCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheMirrorGenieCannotBeCommandedCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The mirror genie cannot be commanded"@en, "Der Spiegelgeist lässt sich nicht befehligen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The dual mirror resembles a wish-granting genie, but unlike the fairytale one it cannot be ordered about, petitioned or moved to pity; it complies willingly only once one declares one's intention."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingDualMirrorCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDoNotGiveFateToMirrorMakersCh18 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not give your fate to the mirror makers"@en, "Das Schicksal nicht den Spiegelmachern überlassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mirror makers try to persuade the dot that it must travel one fixed line, which holds only if the dot accepts it; the whole world is beyond one's reach, yet one's own layer is wholly at one's disposal, so be the Maker of your fate by intending it and do not hand it over to them."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingMirrorMakersCh18 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XVIII The Mirror World, section 'The League of Mirror Makers'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V:
# Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), part 2: chapter XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity
# and the afterword A Strange Reality.
#
# Two independent extraction passes ran over the text (A 227 records, B 177;
# 15 records of B without counterpart in A: 1 added, 13 covered, 1 not owed).
# The record added from B, the author's ordering of the amplifiers of
# visualisation from the body text, replaces pass A's list of ten techniques,
# which was taken from the chapter-end summary. A reader of the whole part
# added 5 nodes (high vitality mirroring a successful person; the frame of
# intention as concept beside its practice; the temerity to assert one's
# right and an elementary foundation of knowledge, both as the prior steps the
# passes had linked wrongly; the book yielding awareness and adeptness rather
# than Knowledge). Corrected: the receiving record became a concept, since the
# author claims his wording and systematisation as his own; the two disputes
# (special relativity, mechanistic science) are concepts, only the author's
# side being read; Jung and Bell are not namings and sit inside the concepts
# that cite them. Section headings were checked against the text; the
# afterword has no heading until 'The Intention of the Ancient Magicians'.
#
# Stupen' I to IV are not restated: 9 records whose claim a node there already
# carries are left out and linked (pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11,
# pmc:TranserfingInspirationX10,
# pmc:TranserfingThoughtProgrammedEnergyRealizesAlternativesCh11,
# pmc:TranserfingPendulumsCh16, pmc:TranserfingIndigoArrivalsCh16,
# pmp:TranserfingTransurfingRuleCh16, pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma,
# pmc:TranserfingClairvoyance, pmc:TranserfingWhyClairvoyantsErr); 28 nodes
# that restate an earlier node with a difference say so in a note.
#
# Shared system terms typed here: pmc:TranserfingGatekeeperCh19,
# pmc:TranserfingRightOfTheMakerCh19, pmc:TranserfingFrameOfIntentionCh19.
# The terms of part 1 (pmc:TranserfingDualMirrorCh18,
# pmc:TranserfingMirrorPrinciplesCh18, pmc:TranserfingAmalgamCh18) are named in
# notes and not typed here.
#


#
# ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'
#

pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Control of reality"@en, "Steuerung der Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The overall faculty Transurfing claims: shaping the layer of one's own world by focused intention and thought so that the world's mirror returns the image chosen."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingSteeringRealityWithoutDirectForceCh16: control is framed here through the dual mirror: one shapes the layer of one's world by an image held in thought, which the mirror reflects."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoodEnergyBeforeAnyTransurfingCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Good energy before any Transurfing"@en, "Gute Energie vor jedem Transurfing"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sound energy levels are named the first indispensable condition of the whole method."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without it Transurfing is said to be entirely impossible."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTwoKindsOfEnergyCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two kinds of energy"@en, "Zwei Arten von Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author distinguishes physiological energy, felt as warmth and bodily strength and produced by metabolism, from free energy, which streams in from the cosmos along energy channels, shows as vigour, and is identified with the energy of intention and with life force."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingEnergiyaNamereniya: free energy is said here to stream in from the cosmos along the energy channels and is equated with life force; physiological energy is said to need nothing beyond food, rest, exercise and fresh air."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPhysiologicalEnergyCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Physiological energy"@en, "Physiologische Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bodily warmth and strength sustained by metabolism."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingMaintainingPhysiologicalEnergyCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Maintaining physiological energy"@en, "Physiologische Energie erhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep bodily energy up by eating properly, resting, taking exercise and getting fresh air."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBasicCareYieldsPhysiologicalEnergyCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Basic care yields physiological energy"@en, "Grundpflege ergibt physiologische Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Food, rest, exercise and fresh air are said to suffice for physiological energy."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingMaintainingPhysiologicalEnergyCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingPhysiologicalEnergyCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSignOfVeryLowEnergyCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign of very low energy"@en, "Zeichen sehr niedriger Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Daily toil with strength only for routine tasks, and above all apathy towards life, indicate extremely low energy levels."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: daily toil with strength only for routine tasks, and above all apathy towards life, indicate extremely low energy levels; it bears on pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergyBeforeLateLifeCreativityCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Energy before late-life creativity"@en, "Energie vor Schaffenskraft im Alter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creative work at any age depends on maintaining energy."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingCreatingMasterpiecesAtAnyAgeCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCreatingMasterpiecesAtAnyAgeCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating masterpieces at any age"@en, "Meisterwerke in jedem Alter"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author holds that whoever keeps energy at the right level can produce top creative work regardless of age, not only in youth."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCeasingToStriveAgesAPersonCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Ceasing to strive ages a person"@en, "Aufhören zu streben lässt altern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Life force and creative energy wither once a person stops striving; those who meet the world with satiated indifference age early, and refusing to wonder or seek new ideas brings not just standstill but degradation."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingKeepingWonderAliveCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping wonder alive"@en, "Staunen wachhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep regarding the world wide-eyed, keep wondering at it and keep reaching for new ideas."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWonderYieldsEnergyCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Wonder yields energy"@en, "Staunen ergibt Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sustained wonder at the world is said to bring more energy."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingKeepingWonderAliveCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLifeAsProcessWithoutStandstillCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Life as process without standstill"@en, "Leben als Prozess ohne Stillstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Life moves forward or backward but never pauses; nature knows no total rest, so stopping development means decline."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHitchingEnergyToAGoalThroughActionCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Hitching energy to a goal through action"@en, "Energie durch Handeln an ein Ziel koppeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tie the energy of intention to a goal and start dynamic action; when apathetic, begin doing something, anything, as an initial push. Action creates intention, intention kindles life force, in a feedback loop."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDynamicActionYieldsEnergyOfIntentionCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dynamic action yields energy of intention"@en, "Tätigkeit ergibt Absichtsenergie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Energy is said to come once one sets about doing something."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingHitchingEnergyToAGoalThroughActionCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAbundantEnergyBoundInTwoBurdensCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Abundant energy bound in two burdens"@en, "Reichliche Energie in zwei Lasten gebunden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Energy from the cosmos is unlimited and has likely already been taken in full; it is spent on carrying two loads: self-imposed limitations, obligations, conditions and promises (each a plummet round the neck), and the load of excess potential from over-valuing things (inferiority, guilt and duty, exaggerated complexity of problems)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAccumulatedObligationsEndInCrisisCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Accumulated obligations end in crisis"@en, "Gehäufte Verpflichtungen enden in der Krise"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the weights grow too many a crisis follows: illness, depression or some tragedy; the person turns fearful and mistrustful, and reality darkens accordingly for a long stretch."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnrealisedGoalDoesNotActivateEnergyCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unrealised goal does not activate energy"@en, "Unverwirklichtes Ziel aktiviert keine Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only a goal being carried out activates intention energy; one left hanging at the planning stage becomes another weight drawing energy."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: only a goal being carried out activates intention energy; one left hanging at the planning stage becomes another weight drawing energy; it bears on pmp:TranserfingHitchingEnergyToAGoalThroughActionCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingToxinsNarrowTheEnergyChannelsCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Toxins narrow the energy channels"@en, "Schlacken verengen die Energiekanäle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accumulated toxins clog the energy channels like scale in an old pipe, cutting the flow of free energy to a trickle and causing poor physical condition, low creativity and illness."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingCloggedBodyAndChronicStressRestrictMeridiansCh11: toxins alone are named here, likened to scale in an old pipe, and the shrunken flow is said to feed mostly useless weights, leaving little for vitality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReserveOfVitalityCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reserve of vitality"@en, "Vitalitätsreserve"@de ;
    skos:definition "What remains after channels and weights have taken their share is the vitality reserve, the source of alertness, initiative, optimism and the sense of being able to move mountains; one can gauge it from one's condition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFreeingUpResourcesCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Freeing up resources"@en, "Ressourcen freisetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ask what oppresses you; compile a list of the weights; drop the many that can go without regret and either carry out or strike the rest; in particular remove things endlessly postponed (self-demands such as always being best, vows like quitting smoking or learning a language from next Monday)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingForcedQuittingSpendsEnergyTwiceCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Forced quitting spends energy twice"@en, "Erzwungenes Aufgeben kostet doppelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "While trying to give up a bad habit one pays the pendulum its interest and also carries the obligation to quit, so energy is spent twice and the struggle can last years."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingFreeingUpResourcesCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingConvictionInsteadOfCompulsionWithHabitsCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Conviction instead of compulsion with habits"@en, "Überzeugung statt Zwang bei Gewohnheiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Either give the habit up decisively out of conviction, or lift the obligation and steer the habit into a measured, civilised form (a good pipe and quality tobacco instead of scrounged cigarettes, a decent hip flask instead of secret drinking), building a partnership with the creditor; first look at yourself honestly about what you are doing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVolitionAndDeclarationsWorsenAHabitCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Volition and declarations worsen a habit"@en, "Willenskraft und Erklärungen verschlimmern die Gewohnheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pushing oneself into a corner by willpower raises tension and inevitably leads to crisis; announcing the intention at this stage only makes things worse; the author concedes the civilising route is not an ideal solution."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingConvictionInsteadOfCompulsionWithHabitsCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCrammingIsADeadWeightCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Cramming is a dead weight"@en, "Pauken ist totes Gewicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intending to fill one's head with information creates heavy tension without realising intention; memorising is pointless baggage costing disproportionate energy."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingKnowledgeAssimilatedInActionCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKnowledgeAssimilatedInActionCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowledge assimilated in action"@en, "Im Handeln angeeignetes Wissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowledge, unlike stored data, properly absorbed through use, without the burden of memorising."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLearningThroughRealisedIntentionCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Learning through realised intention"@en, "Lernen durch verwirklichte Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Assimilate knowledge in action through concrete cases of realised intention; e.g. instead of explaining lessons to children, have them teach the lesson to you, turning passive intent into active intent."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingActiveIntentYieldsAssimilatedKnowledgeCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Active intent yields assimilated knowledge"@en, "Aktive Absicht ergibt angeeignetes Wissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Redirecting intention from passive to active is said to make the burden of memorising drop away at once."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLearningThroughRealisedIntentionCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingKnowledgeAssimilatedInActionCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreeingResourcesYieldsEnergyOfIntentionCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Freeing resources yields energy of intention"@en, "Freisetzen ergibt Absichtsenergie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dropping weights is said to release intention energy reserves at once."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFreeingUpResourcesCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFindingOnesOwnInnermostGoalCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding one's own innermost goal"@en, "Das eigene innerste Ziel finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Discovering one's true goal, upon which heart and mind rush towards it with enthusiasm and the energy deficit ceases."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergyBeforeSearchingForOnesGoalCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Energy before searching for one's goal"@en, "Energie vor der Zielsuche"@de ;
    skos:definition "The search for the own goal needs free energy, which should be the first priority; without the ability to act, determining the goal is pointless."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingEnergyReservesBeforeHearingHeartsDesireX10: the order is stated as a necessity with a consequence: in a weak state pendulums impose their own goals."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingFindingOnesOwnInnermostGoalCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Pendulums are likely to exploit the weakness and impose their own goals."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumsImposeGoalsOnTheWeakCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums impose goals on the weak"@en, "Pendel drängen Schwachen Ziele auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "In a weak state pendulums are likely to exploit it and press their own goals on the person."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingFindingOnesOwnInnermostGoalCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromObligationsBeforeFindingTheGoalCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from obligations before finding the goal"@en, "Freiheit von Verpflichtungen vor der Zielfindung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Finding the own goal requires first some freedom from obligations and release of the final weight of needing a goal."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingFindingOnesOwnInnermostGoalCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingPermittingOneselfNoGoalForNowCh19 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPermittingOneselfNoGoalForNowCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Permitting oneself no goal for now"@en, "Sich vorerst kein Ziel erlauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gain a degree of freedom from obligations to others and oneself, and as the last weight allow yourself to have no personal goal for now."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeMethodsOfRaisingEnergyCh19 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three methods of raising energy"@en, "Drei Wege zur Energiesteigerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author names three methods to raise energy: freeing up resources, exercising the energy channels, widening the meridians; he then calls body cleansing with natural food the most direct route."@en ;
    skos:note "Members: pmp:TranserfingFreeingUpResourcesCh19, pmp:TranserfingEnergyExercisesWithProcessVisualisationCh19, pmp:TranserfingCleansingTheBodyAndARawNaturalDietCh19."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInfluxOfStrengthFromFreedResourcesCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Influx of strength from freed resources"@en, "Kraftzufluss aus freigesetzten Ressourcen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced result: a tangible surge of strength; energy once spent on pendulums of alcohol or tobacco, stress, doubt, guilt and proving significance turns into resolve and becomes available income."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingFreeingUpResourcesCh19, pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergyExercisesYieldEnergyOfIntentionCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Energy exercises yield energy of intention"@en, "Energieübungen ergeben Absichtsenergie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Exercising the channels is said to raise intention energy as achieving goals does, like training muscles."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEnergyExercisesWithProcessVisualisationCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnergyAtrophiesWhenLifeCalmsCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Energy atrophies when life calms"@en, "Energie verkümmert bei ruhigem Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once the main peaks are conquered and life flows calmly, intention energy declines."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingEnergyExercisesWithProcessVisualisationCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Energy exercises with process visualisation"@en, "Energieübungen mit Prozessvisualisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "During any physical exercise attend to the ascending and descending energy currents; add a mental slide of your reserve of intention energy growing every day; work methodically and daily affirm that your intention energy grows each day."@en ;
    skos:note "Compensates the fall in energy once main goals are reached; the energy then rises on its own once induced."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingAttendingToTheCentralMeridiansDuringExerciseCh11: the attention to the currents is combined with a slide of one's intention energy growing day by day and a daily spoken affirmation, as a remedy for the fall in energy once main goals are reached."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFatigueTheDayAfterIntenseEnergyWorkCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Fatigue the day after intense energy work"@en, "Müdigkeit am Tag nach intensiver Energiearbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "After intense energy exercise one feels broken, tired and downcast the next day, like muscle ache after a training break; the author says it passes and is no cause for worry."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingEnergyExercisesWithProcessVisualisationCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBoostAfterAFewSessionsCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Boost after a few sessions"@en, "Schub nach wenigen Sitzungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: after a few sessions such a surge of energy that one wants to leap and fly."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingEnergyExercisesWithProcessVisualisationCh19, pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCleansingTheBodyAndARawNaturalDietCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cleansing the body and a raw natural diet"@en, "Körperreinigung und naturbelassene Rohkost"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cleanse the body physiologically and change to natural food not treated with heat, then keep the body in that clean state."@en ;
    skos:note "Meditation is mentioned as an alternative way of flushing the channels under high pressure, called long and complex; the author recommends physiological cleansing instead. The diet theme is deferred to later."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCleansingYieldsEnergyFlowCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Cleansing yields energy flow"@en, "Reinigung ergibt Energiefluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "A cleansed body is likened to a clean pipe with strong water pressure; called the most direct route to higher energy."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCleansingTheBodyAndARawNaturalDietCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyBeforeInspirationCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "High energy before inspiration"@en, "Hohe Energie vor Inspiration"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inspiration is presented as the result of high energy levels."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingInspirationX10 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingScepticismAndApathyShowLowEnergyCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Scepticism and apathy show low energy"@en, "Skepsis und Apathie zeigen niedrige Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Scepticism and apathy betray an energy deficit; the resulting pessimism is at once streamed into physical reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: scepticism and apathy betray an energy deficit; the resulting pessimism is at once streamed into physical reality; it bears on pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHighVitalityMirrorsASuccessfulPersonCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "High vitality mirrors a successful person"@en, "Hohe Vitalität spiegelt einen Erfolgreichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "With vitality high, a person is said to send the world's mirror the picture of someone who succeeds, and success then approaches without being chased; low energy instead colours the view with pessimism that streams at once into reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEuphoriaBuildsCastlesInTheAirCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Euphoria builds castles in the air"@en, "Euphorie baut Luftschlösser"@de ;
    skos:definition "Peaks of seeming inspiration quickly burn out into pragmatism and gloom; this is euphoria, not inspiration, and the ideas it yields soon look hopeless."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingInspirationX10 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEuphoriaVersusInspirationCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Euphoria versus inspiration"@en, "Euphorie gegenüber Inspiration"@de ;
    skos:definition "A sudden jump from low to high energy (stimulants, exciting news) opens the mind to regions of the alternatives space remote from what is materialised; such ideas need far more energy to realise and fade quickly, like brilliant dream ideas on waking. Real ideas arise from stable intention energy and lie near the alternatives flow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSteadyEnergyOrGiftBeforeRealisableIdeasCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Steady energy or gift before realisable ideas"@en, "Stetige Energie oder Gabe vor verwirklichbaren Ideen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To touch such ideas one needs either a special gift or consistently high energy."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingReachingRealisableIdeasCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReachingRealisableIdeasCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reaching realisable ideas"@en, "Verwirklichbare Ideen erreichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The conscious mind touching ideas beyond the material world that are close to the alternatives flow and can be realised; consistently high energy is said to make up for lacking a special gift."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMaterialisationIsNotInstantaneousCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Materialisation is not instantaneous"@en, "Materialisierung geschieht nicht sofort"@de ;
    skos:definition "For a reflection to form one needs either a sharp image arising when heart and mind agree, or prolonged deliberate concentration; otherwise life would be chaos like a computer game."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingControllingOnesLayerAsOneControlsTheBodyCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Controlling one's layer as one controls the body"@en, "Die eigene Weltschicht wie den Körper lenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "A faculty the author says has fully atrophied but can be regained: steering one's world once one feels at one with it, as one moves one's own body."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOnenessYieldsControlOfTheLayerCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Oneness yields control of the layer"@en, "Einssein ergibt Lenkung der Schicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Feeling one with the world is said to bring the ability to steer it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCultivatingOnenessWithTheWorldCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingControllingOnesLayerAsOneControlsTheBodyCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCultivatingOnenessWithTheWorldCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Cultivating oneness with the world"@en, "Einssein mit der Welt pflegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Regard yourself as master of your reality as of your body; adopt reality's pace and expect no instant change, staying calm, patient and goal-focused; keep attending to your circumstances, feel part of the world, in context with it, seek what links you to it: a separate particle and dissolved in it at once."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOnenessCannotBeTaughtCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Oneness cannot be taught"@en, "Einssein ist nicht lehrbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author admits the task is hard, cannot be taught, comes only through everyday living and may take a lifetime; for those unwilling to do such spiritual work he offers simpler instructions."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCultivatingOnenessWithTheWorldCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingYouReceiveWhatIntentionIsAimedAtCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "You receive what intention is aimed at"@en, "Man erhält, worauf die Absicht zielt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Results may not be immediate, but one always gets what intention was focused on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAimingAttentionAtTheResultSlideCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Aiming attention at the result slide"@en, "Aufmerksamkeit auf das Ergebnisbild richten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hold attention on a slide of the desired result: growing muscles when building muscle, a leaner body when losing weight, the energy channels and energy body when raising energy; aim at the goal, not the effort."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUndirectedOrEffortFocusedExerciseCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Undirected or effort-focused exercise"@en, "Ungerichtete oder anstrengungsfixierte Übung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intention aimed at nothing gets nothing; exercise without a set purpose wastes effort; attention on effort instead of goal spends only physiological energy and keeps one forever on the path, since the mirror shows the image's content."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: intention aimed at nothing gets nothing; exercise without a set purpose wastes effort; attention on effort instead of goal spends only physiological energy and keeps one forever on the path, since the mirror shows the image's content; it bears on pmp:TranserfingAimingAttentionAtTheResultSlideCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnfocusedEnergyIsUselessCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Unfocused energy is useless"@en, "Ungebündelte Energie ist nutzlos"@de ;
    skos:definition "High vitality without direction is scattered like children's energy; like a lamp versus a laser it must be bundled towards a goal to work."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThoughtRuleYieldsCommandOfThoughtsCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Thought rule yields command of thoughts"@en, "Gedankenregel ergibt Gedankenherrschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the simple rule develops control of thought as a habit."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingControllingTheTrainOfThoughtCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingCommandOfOnesThoughtsCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingControllingTheTrainOfThoughtCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Controlling the train of thought"@en, "Den Gedankenfluss lenken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rule: train yourself to keep your thoughts on your present activity; do nothing aimlessly; proclaim a declaration of intention that the mind wanders only when you allow it, so you can deliberately return to concentration; concentration means focus, not tension."@en ;
    skos:note "Awkward at first, becomes habit with time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSystematicReturnToTheTargetSlideCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Systematic return to the target slide"@en, "Systematische Rückkehr zum Zielbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Systematically focus attention on the target slide; when thoughts drift, make a habit of bringing them back again and again, until the slide is a constant background companion; a perfect unity of heart and mind at all times is not required."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCommandOfOnesThoughtsCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Command of one's thoughts"@en, "Herrschaft über die Gedanken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping thoughts under control and returning to concentration at will, which the author says subjects reality to one's will."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTargetSlideYieldsRealisedGoalCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Target slide yields realised goal"@en, "Zielbild ergibt verwirklichtes Ziel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author asserts the image will take shape and the world's mirror will reflect it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSystematicReturnToTheTargetSlideCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLayerOfTheWorldAndItsHueCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Layer of the world and its hue"@en, "Weltschicht und ihr Farbton"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mirror is many-layered: each being has its own mirror plate from birth, its thoughts and intentions build an image reflected as a separate reality; all layers together form observed physical reality. One creates the layer by thought and action; Transurfing treats only the metaphysical side. What counts is the layer's hue, how well things go; negative thinking darkens it and resentment darkens it further through feedback."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingLayerOfOnesWorld: the layer is set on the dual mirror as one mirror plate per being from birth, and its decisive quality is its hue, how well things go, which negative thought darkens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingKeepingTheLayerCleanCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping the layer clean"@en, "Die Schicht sauber halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keep individual reality clean like the body: decisively and at once expel every negative thought before it can spoil your world, as one takes out rubbish."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInnerJunkThatTheWorldTakesAlongCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner junk that the world takes along"@en, "Innerer Ballast, den die Welt mitnimmt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hard-to-remove junk: guilt, inferiority, doubt, stress, fear, discontent, hostility, gloomy expectations; a parable of a person and the world on a magic bus shows the world taking aboard whatever the anxious mind attends to until the journey is ruined."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSymptomsOfGuiltCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Symptoms of guilt"@en, "Symptome der Schuld"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the world seems to punish, mock or undermine you, you show the symptoms of the guilt disease, said to be the most destructive junk whether conscious or not."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingGuiltGeneratesPunishmentCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGuiltGeneratesPunishmentCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Guilt generates punishment"@en, "Schuld erzeugt Strafe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Guilt draws punishment from small mishaps to accidents because outer intention writes retribution into the script per the template worldview; it strains polarisation so balancing forces strike, and attracts manipulators. Guilt is implanted in childhood by manipulative carers as an unconscious chip of duty and atonement."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingPunishmentScript: guilt is also said to strain polarisation and draw manipulators, and to be implanted in childhood like a microchip of duty and atonement."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGuiltCannotBeSuppressedCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Guilt cannot be suppressed"@en, "Schuld lässt sich nicht unterdrücken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Guilt is too deeply instilled to suppress or simply discard; convincing oneself of owing nothing does not help."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCeasingToJustifyOneselfCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCeasingToJustifyOneselfCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ceasing to justify oneself"@en, "Aufhören, sich zu rechtfertigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stop justifying yourself: watch your actions with awareness; replace habitual apologising over trifles with explaining actions only when strictly necessary; let the guilt feeling stay inside but do not show it; if truly guilty, ask forgiveness only once."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingRefusingGuilt: no self-persuasion is asked for; the guilt may stay inside, only its outward show stops, and the outer form is said to tidy the inner content by feedback."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingManipulatorsWithdrawCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Manipulators withdraw"@en, "Manipulatoren ziehen sich zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced signs: manipulators leave once they get no more output; heart and mind grow used to not justifying; reasons for atonement become fewer."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingCeasingToJustifyOneselfCh19, pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromGuiltCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNonJustificationYieldsFreedomFromGuiltCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Non-justification yields freedom from guilt"@en, "Nicht-Rechtfertigung ergibt Schuldfreiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "External form, through feedback, tidies up inner content."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCeasingToJustifyOneselfCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromGuiltCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromGuiltCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from guilt"@en, "Freiheit von Schuld"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state in which guilt and the problems tied to it have vanished and manipulators no longer get a hold."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImportanceShrinksAsItIsStressedCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Importance shrinks as it is stressed"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit schwindet, wenn man sie betont"@de ;
    skos:definition "A law likened to quantum uncertainty: significance falls to the degree it is emphasised; who does not care about it has it automatically; striving to prove oneself is a chase after the reflection round the mirror circle."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDroppingImportanceYieldsSelfEsteemCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping importance yields self-esteem"@en, "Bedeutungsverzicht ergibt Selbstwert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Here the cause removes the effect through feedback."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingGivingUpRaisingOnesSignificanceCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHealthySelfEsteemCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingGivingUpRaisingOnesSignificanceCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Giving up raising one's significance"@en, "Aufgeben, die eigene Bedeutung zu steigern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Consciously redirect intention: drop every attempt to prove yourself, show off or raise your own significance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOthersSenseSignificanceAndRespectItCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Others sense significance and respect it"@en, "Andere spüren den Wert und achten ihn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: people around intuitively sense no need for confirmation, are drawn closer and show more respect; the mirror circle stops, turns and comes towards you."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingGivingUpRaisingOnesSignificanceCh19, pmc:TranserfingHealthySelfEsteemCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHealthySelfEsteemCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healthy self-esteem"@en, "Gesundes Selbstwertgefühl"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-esteem as if there had never been an inferiority complex, with the conviction of being worth something."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFearTurnsDesireIntoLongingCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Fear turns desire into longing"@en, "Angst verwandelt Wunsch in Sehnsucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doubts, stress and fear, once mirrored, bring something truly fearful into the layer; anxiety turns desire into longing, raises outer importance and lowers the odds of success."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWaitingThatFeelsLikeLongingCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Waiting that feels like longing"@en, "Warten als Sehnsucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any waiting that has the quality of longing leads nowhere and must be abandoned."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: any waiting that has the quality of longing leads nowhere and must be abandoned; it bears on pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSafetyNetAndAcceptingDefeatBeforehandCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Safety net and accepting defeat beforehand"@en, "Sicherheitsnetz und Niederlage vorab annehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To blunt impatience, have a fallback plan in case of failure and accept the possibility of defeat at the start."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingSafetyNet: the net serves here to dull impatience towards a goal, and it is paired with accepting defeat at the outset."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDespairDissolvesInnerImportanceCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Despair dissolves inner importance"@en, "Verzweiflung löst innere Bedeutsamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "When failure hits ambition hard, hopelessness can make one give up and drop self-importance like dead weight."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLightnessAfterDroppingSelfImportanceCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lightness after dropping self-importance"@en, "Leichtigkeit nach Ablegen der Selbstwichtigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: one feels better, free and light at once, and things pick up immediately."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmc:TranserfingHealthySelfEsteemCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFocusingOnTheGoalAsAchievedNotTheRouteCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Focusing on the goal as achieved, not the route"@en, "Auf das erreichte Ziel statt auf den Weg achten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not calculate route and means; concentrate attention on the goal as though already reached, leaving outer intention to open suitable doors when due."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRemedyForDoubtAndFearViaTheMirrorPrinciplesCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Remedy for doubt and fear via the mirror principles"@en, "Mittel gegen Zweifel und Angst über die Spiegelprinzipien"@de ;
    skos:definition "First keep the amalgam that your world looks after you; second keep exactly to the three final mirror principles: accept possible failure (before an exam ask whether failing might be best for you), move with the alternatives flow, do the required work while indifferent to the result and regard any outcome as success; do not ponder by which route the goal arrives, keep visualising the slide and stepping towards it."@en ;
    skos:note "Links the shared terms of part 1: pmc:TranserfingAmalgamCh18 and pmc:TranserfingMirrorPrinciplesCh18."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPretendingNotToWantFailsCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pretending not to want fails"@en, "Vorgetäuschtes Nichtwollen scheitert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Faking indifference to the goal is self-deception and will not work."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingRemedyForDoubtAndFearViaTheMirrorPrinciplesCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingNamingAFailureASuccessCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Naming a failure a success"@en, "Einen Misserfolg Erfolg nennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When you make a wrong step, call the failure a success, relating to the outcome positively instead of the customary negative way."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMirrorPrinciplesYieldFreedomFromFearCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Mirror principles yield freedom from fear"@en, "Spiegelprinzipien ergeben Angstfreiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Refocusing on observing the mirror principles is said to remove fear and doubt."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRemedyForDoubtAndFearViaTheMirrorPrinciplesCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromDoubtAndFearCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRealityVisiblyChangesCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality visibly changes"@en, "Die Wirklichkeit ändert sich sichtbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: once the principles take effect reality changes considerably, the mind becomes convinced the mirror works, and one sees the road to success differs from what one imagined."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingRemedyForDoubtAndFearViaTheMirrorPrinciplesCh19, pmp:TranserfingNamingAFailureASuccessCh19, pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromDoubtAndFearCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreedomFromDoubtAndFearCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from doubt and fear"@en, "Freiheit von Zweifel und Angst"@de ;
    skos:definition "A calmed heart and mind in which fear and doubt have gone and the mind is convinced the mirror works."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCriticismReboundsOnTheCriticCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Criticism rebounds on the critic"@en, "Kritik fällt auf den Kritiker zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any criticism, even justified, is very disadvantageous: balancing forces, restoring the balance of good and bad, put the accuser in the dock; criticism on one's own part should be made taboo."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingModerateCriticism: criticism of one's own is to be made taboo altogether, even when justified, since balancing forces put the accuser in the dock."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingLayerOfTheWorldAndItsHueCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPlayingTheDissatisfactionPerformanceCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Playing the dissatisfaction performance"@en, "Das Stück der Unzufriedenheit spielen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting out the scene of disliking one's world and life creates and sustains exactly that reality; one should keep recalling one stands before a mirror and that amalgam plus the last three mirror principles can turn the layer cosy."@en ;
    skos:note "The amalgam and the last three principles are pmc:TranserfingAmalgamCh18 and pmc:TranserfingMirrorPrinciplesCh18."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingLayerOfTheWorldAndItsHueCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCollectiveWarpAndTheCloudyHazeCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Collective warp and the cloudy haze"@en, "Kollektive Verzerrung und trüber Dunst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shared reality forms where layers overlap; after parties people repay the pendulum, energy deficit fills thought forms with negativity, collective tension warps the mirror, so machines break more often on Mondays and accidents happen at work. Depression or altered awareness draws the layer into murky regions of the alternatives space: surroundings unchanged yet oppressive, hostile, affecting even equipment. A bad patch begins either with bodily ailments from energy deficit or with negative emotions from unmet expectations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRaisedEnergyToKeepHazeOutCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Raised energy to keep haze out"@en, "Erhöhte Energie hält den Dunst fern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping murky areas out of one's reality requires raising energy and keeping the layer clean."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingALayerLedOutOfTheHazeCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without raised energy murky areas are let into one's reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIrritationCeasesAtSufficientVitalityCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Irritation ceases at sufficient vitality"@en, "Reizbarkeit endet bei ausreichender Vitalität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: once vitality reaches the necessary level one no longer feels irritated."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmc:TranserfingHighEnergyLevelsCh11."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStraightenRealityBeforeFollowingPrinciplesCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Straighten reality before following principles"@en, "Erst die Wirklichkeit richten, dann Prinzipien befolgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one is too low to follow principles and is depressed, the first step is to set reality straight by self-care before the rest."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingRemedyForDoubtAndFearViaTheMirrorPrinciplesCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingComfortingTheInnerChildCh19 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingALayerLedOutOfTheHazeCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A layer led out of the haze"@en, "Aus dem Dunst geführte Weltschicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "One's reality brought from the cloudy, oppressive zone of the alternatives space into a clear area, its hues warmer and softer."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingComfortingTheInnerChildCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Comforting the inner child"@en, "Das innere Kind trösten"@de ;
    skos:definition "When down, treat yourself as a crying child to be cared for: do a bit of your favourite activity; take special time to relax without dwelling on distressing problems; go for a walk with your world; buy your favourite treat; give the whole day to yourself and your pleasures; tuck yourself in, telling yourself your world will see to it all."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWarmerHuesTheNextDayCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Warmer hues the next day"@en, "Wärmere Farbtöne am nächsten Tag"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: the next day reality begins to take on warmer, softer hues; the material world visibly changes, the oppressive air lightens, stopped clocks run again, people are drawn to you."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingComfortingTheInnerChildCh19, pmc:TranserfingALayerLedOutOfTheHazeCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfCareLeadsTheLayerOutOfHazeCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Self-care leads the layer out of haze"@en, "Selbstfürsorge führt die Schicht aus dem Dunst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Comforting oneself, together with diligent observance of the mirror principles, is said to bring the layer out of the haze."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingComfortingTheInnerChildCh19 ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRemedyForDoubtAndFearViaTheMirrorPrinciplesCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingALayerLedOutOfTheHazeCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGenerationShiftCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Generation shift"@en, "Generationswechsel"@de ;
    skos:definition "In childhood the layer, like the body, was fresh and its colours bright; growing complaints and negativity in one's thoughts fade its hues until one speaks of the good old days; early Transurfing material calls this the generation shift."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGenerationalLayerShift: the shift is read here in one life: the bright layer of childhood fades as complaints accumulate, and it can be reversed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMirrorPrinciplesRestoreFreshnessCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Mirror principles restore freshness"@en, "Spiegelprinzipien stellen Frische wieder her"@de ;
    skos:definition "Adhering to the mirror principles is said to bring back the original freshness of the layer."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRemedyForDoubtAndFearViaTheMirrorPrinciplesCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRestoredFreshnessOfTheLayerCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRestoredFreshnessOfTheLayerCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Restored freshness of the layer"@en, "Wiederhergestellte Frische der Schicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reversal of the generation shift: former colours, newness of feeling and hope return, giving the full sense of controlling one's own reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Energy of Intention'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'
#

pmc:TranserfingInnerVersusOuterIntentionAndAttributesCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inner versus outer intention and attributes"@en, "Innere gegenüber äußerer Absicht und Attribute"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inner intention, a product of reason, works linearly and controls only what man has made into an attribute of his game (a dammed stretch of river, a donkey driven by force); independent reality obeys only outer intention, born when heart and mind are united. Hence two ways of controlling reality: making things attributes, or working with outer intention in harmony with nature; the author holds civilisation follows the first, less effective path."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingVneshneeNamerenie: inner intention is said to govern only what one has turned into an attribute of one's play, and the two kinds of intention are set out as two paths of civilisation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPolarisationDistortsTheMirrorCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Polarisation distorts the mirror"@en, "Polarisation verzerrt den Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trying to turn the reflection itself with inner intention creates excess potential and balancing forces turn it the other way. Polarisation has two causes: dependent relationships built on comparison, contrast or conditions, and turning the screws, ever more pressure after nothing happens; balancing forces resolve it by colliding opposites so the result is the reverse of what was intended."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAStraightenedMirrorCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A straightened mirror"@en, "Ein gerichteter Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The world responding again instead of acting in reverse, once polarisation is removed."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReleasingSpokesStraightensTheMirrorCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Releasing spokes straightens the mirror"@en, "Speichen lockern richtet den Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Removing polarisation by relaxing the tight side is said to straighten the mirror, a simple matter."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingCorrectingTheMirrorCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAStraightenedMirrorCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingCorrectingTheMirrorCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Correcting the mirror"@en, "Den Spiegel richten"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the world seems to act out of spite: determine what caused the polarisation, find where its opposite poles show, and relax the matching potential, loosening the over-tightened spokes as when truing a bicycle wheel; observe and reason rather than follow habitual approaches."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTurningTheScrewsOnChildrenCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Turning the screws on children"@en, "Bei Kindern die Schrauben anziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Forcing a child to obey as an attribute of the game creates polarisation: the child runs wild or is broken into a compliant component; keeping on tightening loosens other spokes until something breaks."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOvershapingChildren: the harm is explained by the bent wheel: tightening the spokes on one side loosens the other until something breaks."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCorrectingTheMirrorCh19 ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingIndigoArrivalsCh16 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingMixingOrderWithReasonableDisorderCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Mixing order with reasonable disorder"@en, "Ordnung mit vernünftiger Unordnung mischen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Loosen over-tight spokes in a family by deliberate silliness: jumping on beds, pillow fights, howling and odd noises, romping, crawling on all fours, ambushing a family member, smearing jam at table, a muddy puddle in summer; or use British humour that carries seriousness to the absurd. More such sensible foolery is said to make the child more obedient."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingHumour: humour is given here as a family remedy against over-tight order, with romping and British humour, said to make the child more obedient."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSensibleFoolishnessStraightensTheMirrorCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Sensible foolishness straightens the mirror"@en, "Vernünftige Albernheit richtet den Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mischief and humour reduce polarisation and importance, so the child becomes more obedient."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingMixingOrderWithReasonableDisorderCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAStraightenedMirrorCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHumourFreesTheSoulCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Humour frees the soul"@en, "Humor befreit die Seele"@de ;
    skos:definition "Boredom does not exist as such, only the soul's eternal need to control reality; fun feels good because humour and cheer lower importance; the soul squeezed in a vice of excess potential is released when fun eases tension, giving real inner comfort. Reality cannot be shaped while excess potential blocks intention energy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDilutingCoercionWithChoiceAndRespectCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Diluting coercion with choice and respect"@en, "Zwang mit Wahl und Achtung verdünnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without humour one can simply look where the wheel can be relaxed: give a choice within unavoidable demands (dishes or the shop?); base discipline on understood necessity; discuss as equals and model consequences by asking what would happen if; win respect instead of showing power, replace authority with trust; turn a burdensome duty into something that raises the child's importance; apply the Frailing principles."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCoercionYieldsTheOppositeCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Coercion yields the opposite"@en, "Zwang bewirkt das Gegenteil"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coercion bends the mirror and thus produces the reverse result; an adult ruling by prohibition without reasons is a fool with power."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCorrectingTheMirrorCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChoiceAndRespectStraightenTheMirrorCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Choice and respect straighten the mirror"@en, "Wahl und Achtung richten den Spiegel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shifting from power to trust reduces polarisation."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDilutingCoercionWithChoiceAndRespectCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAStraightenedMirrorCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPassiveRoteKnowledgeIsLostCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Passive rote knowledge is lost"@en, "Passives Auswendigwissen geht verloren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowledge taken in by filling the mind and reporting back is stored passively like warehouse goods, loses value fast and is forgotten; the urge to fill the mind provokes refusal."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingLearningByDoingAndTeachingEachOtherCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLearningByDoingAndTeachingEachOtherCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Learning by doing and teaching each other"@en, "Lernen durch Tun und gegenseitiges Lehren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Change teaching from rote learning to learning in practice, and the aim from reporting back to teaching others: pupils alternately play teacher and student."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMutualTeachingYieldsFastAssimilationCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Mutual teaching yields fast assimilation"@en, "Gegenseitiges Lehren ergibt schnelle Aneignung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pupils in such schools are said to master complex curricula brilliantly in record time because intention is set to be active; the author calls the method fully proven."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLearningByDoingAndTeachingEachOtherCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingKnowledgeAssimilatedInActionCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSystemPressurePreventsOutstandingChildrenCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "System pressure prevents outstanding children"@en, "Systemdruck verhindert herausragende Kinder"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pressing a child by every canon of the system makes it a serviceable component; who wants the best for children should constantly watch the polarisation that warps the mirror; intuition deserves priority development."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCorrectingTheMirrorCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotLooseningSpokesTooFarCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not loosening spokes too far"@en, "Speichen nicht zu weit lockern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The spokes must not be slackened excessively either; the golden mean is found by observation and reasoning."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingCorrectingTheMirrorCh19 ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingMixingOrderWithReasonableDisorderCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Correcting the Mirror'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'
#

pmp:TranserfingTargetSlideCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Target slide"@en, "Zielbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualise a picture of the goal already achieved, from inside it: what you do, what you feel, who and what is around you, with yourself at its centre; no strict rules, practise it your own way, keeping in mind that you stand before the mirror shaping an image to be streamed into reality; do not plan the means or impose rigid conditions on the route to the goal; play it as often as you like, at least half an hour daily if the intent is genuine."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingSystematicallyRunningTargetSlideX10: one is to stand inside the picture, not watch it, and to give it at least half an hour a day."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheSlideSetsTheVectorOfTheFlowCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The slide sets the vector of the flow"@en, "Das Bild bestimmt die Richtung des Stroms"@de ;
    skos:definition "Methodically turning the slide over directs the course of events and circumstances towards the goal; right doors open at the right time and one notices them; circumstances work for the goal even when it does not seem so."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTargetSlideYieldsRealisationOfTheGoalCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Target slide yields realisation of the goal"@en, "Zielbild ergibt Verwirklichung des Ziels"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steadily held, the slide is said to aim events towards the goal."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingTargetSlideCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingVisualisingTheProcessCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Visualising the process"@en, "Den Prozess visualisieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once on the path, knowing how the goal will come about and doing what is needed materially, visualise the process on the principle that all goes very well, today better than yesterday, tomorrow better than today."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingVisualisingProcessCh8: process visualisation is reserved for the stage when one is on the way, knows the means and does the material work, and runs on the formula that each day goes better than the last."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOnThePathBeforeProcessVisualisationCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "On the path before process visualisation"@en, "Auf dem Weg vor der Prozessvisualisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Process visualisation applies only after the target is set, one is on the way, has grasped the means and does the material work."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingVisualisingTheProcessCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingTargetSlideCh19 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProcessVisualisationAcceleratesCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Process visualisation accelerates"@en, "Prozessvisualisierung beschleunigt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Visualising the process is said to speed up the realisation."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingVisualisingTheProcessCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAcceleratedRealisationCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceleratedRealisationCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Accelerated realisation"@en, "Beschleunigte Verwirklichung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Speeding up progress towards a goal already under way, likened to rowing in tune with the alternatives flow."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStrengthenedEffectOfTheSlideCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Strengthened effect of the slide"@en, "Verstärkte Wirkung des Zielbilds"@de ;
    skos:definition "A more powerful transmission of thought-programmed energy, hence a stronger effect of visualisation."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAmplifiersOfVisualisationCh19 a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Amplifiers of visualisation"@en, "Verstärker der Visualisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author orders the methods that strengthen the target slide: first the energy currents, next the frame, the explosion wave that enhances the frame, the outer sphere, scenery reduction, and last, for the lazy, the goal amalgam. He later says the variety does not make one technique necessarily stronger than another; one picks the one liked best and judged to work best."@en ;
    skos:note "Members: pmp:TranserfingEnergyCurrentsWithTheSlideCh19, pmp:TranserfingFrameCh19, pmp:TranserfingExplosionWaveCh19, pmp:TranserfingOuterSphereCh19, pmp:TranserfingSceneryReductionCh19, pmp:TranserfingGoalAmalgamCh19."@en ;
    skos:note "Added from pass B in reconciliation; it replaces pass A's list of ten techniques, which was taken from the chapter-end summary."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2006"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCurrentsStrengthenTheSlideCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Currents strengthen the slide"@en, "Ströme verstärken das Zielbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attention on the energy currents is said to increase the force of the transmission."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEnergyCurrentsWithTheSlideCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingStrengthenedEffectOfTheSlideCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingEnergyCurrentsWithTheSlideCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Energy currents with the slide"@en, "Energieströme mit dem Zielbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagine two opposite arrows about a metre long leaving the centre of the body near stomach or solar plexus; turn them at once so the front one points up and the rear one down, turning the key that starts the downward and upward currents; picture effortlessly that they run along the spine in opposite directions into sky and ground; with attention partly on the currents, run the slide as long as you like; best while walking somewhere quiet and empty."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingTurningTheKeyCh14: the arrows are about a metre long, and the key serves here to strengthen the target slide played while attention rests partly on the currents."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFrameOfIntentionCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Frame of intention"@en, "Rahmen der Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "A frame is one characteristic fragment of the target slide, an indispensable attribute of the goal achieved, condensed into a single instant mould: a flash image together with its feeling. It is said to be one more thread connecting one with the goal's sector of the alternatives space and can be strengthened by the explosion wave."@en ;
    skos:note "The text names it simply the frame; the identifier keeps the shared term of this part. The practice of switching it on is pmp:TranserfingFrameCh19."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part, split from the practice so the shared term can be typed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFrameCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The frame"@en, "Der Rahmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pick a characteristic fragment that would be an indispensable part of the goal achieved (rocking chair by the fire, at the helm of one's yacht, planting roses, sealing a deal); turn it over several times until it forms a whole impression, a flash image with its feeling; give it a short title; now and then switch it on in memory for an instant like a light, whenever it occurs to you, without effort."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingFrameInsertingSlideOpenWindowCh9: no window has to be awaited; the frame is switched on for an instant whenever it comes to mind, and it can be given a short title."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheFrameLinksToTheTargetSectorCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The frame links to the target sector"@en, "Der Rahmen verbindet mit dem Zielsektor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The frame is said to be an extra thread to the goal's region of the alternatives space."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFrameCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingStrengthenedEffectOfTheSlideCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingExplosionWaveSendsTheImageOutCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Explosion wave sends the image out"@en, "Explosionswelle sendet das Bild aus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The image is sent into the universe and is said not to be lost; it enhances the frame's effect."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingExplosionWaveCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingStrengthenedEffectOfTheSlideCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingExplosionWaveCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Explosion wave"@en, "Explosionswelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shape a frame or picture you want realised, then at once imagine a sphere bursting outward from you everywhere, as though your energy field had blown apart, as far as you can imagine; repeat until tired of it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheMirrorWorksWithDelayCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The mirror works with delay"@en, "Der Spiegel wirkt verzögert"@de ;
    skos:definition "A thought sent out is not lost, but one must remember the mirror responds with a delay."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingExplosionWaveCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingOuterSphereCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Outer sphere"@en, "Äußere Sphäre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagine a sphere around you that is not yours and pulls at you, stretching your body outward; sense its invisible front some five to seven metres away, which springs back when you stretch or squeeze it; inside is yours, outside is not; hold that feeling, keep part of your attention on it and run the target slide."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLettingTheWorldDoItCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting the world do it"@en, "Die Welt es selbst tun lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instead of moving an object by willpower, imagine the object pulls you along invisible threads and move it through that link; instead of trying to rise, imagine the world itself lifting you; shift from the will commanding the world to allowing the world to act."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingPencilExerciseCh7: the pencil is moved by imagining that it pulls one along invisible threads, and rising into the air by imagining the world lifting one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOuterIntentionMayMoveObjectsCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Outer intention may move objects"@en, "Äußere Absicht kann Dinge bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The reversed imagery is said to give possible partial success."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLettingTheWorldDoItCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingMovingThingsByOuterIntentionCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMovingThingsByOuterIntentionCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Moving things by outer intention"@en, "Dinge durch äußere Absicht bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hedged claim: by turning inner into outer intention one may move a pencil or even rise into the air; the author says one might have some success."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOuterIntentionIsComplexCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Outer intention is complex"@en, "Äußere Absicht ist komplex"@de ;
    skos:definition "Turning will into allowing is quite complex; for slide work it suffices to sense the outer membrane; failure to feel it so far is put down to acting from inner intention."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingOuterSphereCh19 ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingLettingTheWorldDoItCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOuterSphereActsAsAntennaCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Outer sphere acts as antenna"@en, "Äußere Sphäre wirkt als Antenne"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sphere is said to serve as an antenna for thought energy and markedly raise the slide's efficiency."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingOuterSphereCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingStrengthenedEffectOfTheSlideCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSceneryReductionCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Scenery reduction"@en, "Kulissenreduktion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reduce every thought to the common denominator of the goal: finish each logical chain of thought with a fragment of the slide; keep recalling what you aim at and return attention to it whatever you do; make the slide a background image in whose context all events and information are perceived; look at your surroundings through the slide (walking in a park, see the trees as the garden of your future house)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSceneryReductionShapesTheLayerCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Scenery reduction shapes the layer"@en, "Kulissenreduktion formt die Schicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The layer is said to be shaped more effectively and intention manifested."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSceneryReductionCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSceneTakesOnTheGoalsHuesCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Scene takes on the goal's hues"@en, "Die Szene nimmt die Farben des Ziels an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: the present scene feels transformed, with new hues, as if one were virtually already there; then materialisation is said to intensify."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingSceneryReductionCh19, pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingChildhoodCosinessAsKeyCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Childhood cosiness as key"@en, "Kindliche Geborgenheit als Schlüssel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Find what you associate with the calm, cosy feeling of childhood when the world looked after you; use that association as the key for scenery reduction and recall the carefree setting from time to time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingChildhoodKeyYieldsAFriendlyWorldCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Childhood key yields a friendly world"@en, "Kindheitsschlüssel ergibt freundliche Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recalling the childhood setting gradually makes the world friendly again."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingChildhoodCosinessAsKeyCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAFriendlyComfortableWorldCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAFriendlyComfortableWorldCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A friendly, comfortable world"@en, "Eine freundliche, behagliche Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "One's world becoming friendly and comfortable again, taking care of one as in childhood."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingGoalAmalgamCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Goal amalgam"@en, "Zielamalgam"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the lazy: hand the work to your world; ask it to carry you and see to realising your choice; tell yourself that though you do not know how, everything will come right; then relax and simply enjoy the slide without obligation, now and then reminding the world what you expect; still do on the physical plane whatever the goal requires."@en ;
    skos:note "The goal amalgam is a variant of pmc:TranserfingAmalgamCh18, aimed at one goal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingForcedVisualisationIsNullifiedCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forced visualisation is nullified"@en, "Erzwungene Visualisierung wird zunichte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pushing oneself joylessly to turn the slide creates excess potential and balancing forces reduce the work to nothing; then hand the task over to the world."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: pushing oneself joylessly to turn the slide creates excess potential and balancing forces reduce the work to nothing; then hand the task over to the world; it bears on pmp:TranserfingTargetSlideCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoalAmalgamLetsOuterIntentionRealiseCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Goal amalgam lets outer intention realise"@en, "Zielamalgam lässt äußere Absicht verwirklichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Declaring that intention programs the world to unfold events towards the goal, loosening one's grip for outer intention."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingGoalAmalgamCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoFloatingInCloudsCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No floating in clouds"@en, "Nicht in den Wolken schweben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Resting in the arms of the world does not excuse inaction; physical steps towards the goal remain owed."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingGoalAmalgamCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingGivingFocusToIntentionCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Giving focus to intention"@en, "Der Absicht Halt geben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whatever the technique, express firm intention, not a wish, seeing the goal as inevitable: say 'I have', or at least 'I plan to have'; take concrete actions confirming seriousness (setting an alarm; for a house, act as if moving in soon, study adverts and catalogues, choose furniture and appliances, look into all that moving involves); self-made hooks or rituals may hold the intention but are optional."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingATalismansPowerLiesInTheRelationshipCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A talisman's power lies in the relationship"@en, "Die Kraft des Talismans liegt in der Beziehung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Folk rituals (touching wood, salt over the shoulder, clover charms for luck and against evil) work not through special properties of objects but because belief in them focuses intention."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingRitualAsProp: the power is placed in one's relationship to the object, which focuses intention; clover charms and touching wood are the examples."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFocusedIntentionIsPowerfulCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Focused intention is powerful"@en, "Gebündelte Absicht ist mächtig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Concrete confirming actions are said to make intention very powerful."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingGivingFocusToIntentionCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingChoosingAndDosingTechniquesCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Choosing and dosing techniques"@en, "Techniken wählen und dosieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Use one technique or several at once, choosing the one you like most and think works best; avoid both zeal and sloppiness; take as rule that any outcome is the right one; feel no inner discomfort; live inside the slide, not watching it from outside; never try too hard; regularly enjoy thoughts of the goal achieved and its consequences, setting up a self-reinforcing circle of pleasure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnityOfHeartAndMindBeforeOuterIntentionCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Unity of heart and mind before outer intention"@en, "Einheit von Herz und Verstand vor äußerer Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outer intention, and so the effect of visualisation, needs heart and mind to agree; forcing a compulsory task prevents that unity."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingHeartMindUnityBeforeControlOuterCh9: the dependent step is the effect of visualisation, and the consequence is named: forced practice prevents the unity and gets nowhere."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Forced practice gets nowhere and is a waste of time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDiffuseThoughtsProduceNothingCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Diffuse thoughts produce nothing"@en, "Zerstreute Gedanken bewirken nichts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thoughts left to drift dissolve without visible result; only worst fears, which fill the mind, come true; few have systematically aimed their thoughts at a goal even for a month; success loves regularity."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: thoughts left to drift dissolve without visible result; only worst fears, which fill the mind, come true; few have systematically aimed their thoughts at a goal even for a month; success loves regularity; it bears on pmp:TranserfingTargetSlideCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImpatienceAfterASingleWishCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Impatience after a single wish"@en, "Ungeduld nach einem einzigen Wunsch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like someone giving up on a newly planted apple tree for not fruiting at once, people abandon goals too soon; reality cannot be shaped by a single wish."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: like someone giving up on a newly planted apple tree for not fruiting at once, people abandon goals too soon; reality cannot be shaped by a single wish; it bears on pmp:TranserfingTargetSlideCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTransitZonesAndRipplesInRealityCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transit zones and ripples in reality"@en, "Transitzonen und Kräuseln der Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Normally the layer follows the flow of least energy; intense visualisation straightens the stream towards the goal and carries the layer through intermediate transit zones of the alternatives space, usually met in dreams, with unnatural scripts and scenery; reality is deformed like disturbed water."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRipplesInRealityAfterIntenseVisualisationCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ripples in reality after intense visualisation"@en, "Kräuseln der Wirklichkeit nach intensiver Visualisierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign: the day after enthusiastic practice one meets oddly tall, strangely dressed or ugly people, needless irritability and conflict, a dreamlike strangeness; the author denies this is chance or magnetic storms."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingTargetSlideCh19, pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAmalgamVersusTheMakersIntentionCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Amalgam versus the Maker's intention"@en, "Amalgam gegenüber der Absicht des Schöpfers"@de ;
    skos:definition "The amalgam alone suffices to make one's layer cosy; combining the Maker's intention with the other techniques achieves far more, illustrated by one toddler pushed by its world and another leading its world by the hand."@en ;
    skos:note "Graded force stands against the later remark that no technique is necessarily stronger than another (pmc:TranserfingAmplifiersOfVisualisationCh19)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingIntegrationOfIntentionCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Integration of intention"@en, "Integration der Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hold an integral feeling that all is wonderful and proceeding as it ought; if maintained, this alone is said to suffice and the techniques can be dropped."@en ;
    skos:note "Drawn from a reader's letter the author interprets."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIntegrationReflectsAGeneralImageOfSuccessCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Integration reflects a general image of success"@en, "Integration spiegelt ein Gesamtbild des Erfolgs"@de ;
    skos:definition "The integral feeling creates an overall image of success that reality reflects; potential is limited only by intention."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingIntegrationOfIntentionCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingControlOfRealityCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Reality Maker'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Coordinating the dream'
#

pmc:TranserfingInsideAndOutsideTheMirrorCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Inside and outside the mirror"@en, "Innerhalb und außerhalb des Spiegels"@de ;
    skos:definition "Life is a daydream that circumstances hypnotise one into and that attention on the reflection keeps consolidating (the poor grow poorer); inside the mirror is non-lucid dreaming where reality governs you, as in a game whose rules others set and which you cannot leave; outside is lucid dreaming. Only attention keeps one locked in; touching the reflection to change it is an illusion, possible only from the outer side where inner turns into outer intention."@en ;
    skos:note "The mirror is pmc:TranserfingDualMirrorCh18."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Coordinating the dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingEscapingTheMirrorCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Escaping the mirror"@en, "Aus dem Spiegel treten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Move attention off the reflection onto the image, becoming aware that a mirror is before you; then, per the fifth principle, turn the chain of thoughts from unwanted to wanted, from dislike to liking, from sickness to health, from the means to the final goal; change your relationship rather than resisting events."@en ;
    skos:note "The fifth principle belongs to pmc:TranserfingMirrorPrinciplesCh18; the mirror is pmc:TranserfingDualMirrorCh18."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Coordinating the dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSwitchingAttentionYieldsTheOuterPositionCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Switching attention yields the outer position"@en, "Aufmerksamkeitswechsel ergibt die Außenposition"@de ;
    skos:definition "Awareness of standing before the mirror is said to grant the power to mould reality after an image."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingEscapingTheMirrorCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingBeingOutsideTheMirrorCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Coordinating the dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBeingOutsideTheMirrorCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being outside the mirror"@en, "Außerhalb des Spiegels sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lucid waking dream: no longer prisoner of the game, life unfolds according to one's will, one throws the dice instead of being a chip, and reality is found pliable to one's mental image."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Coordinating the dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDeclaringAnUnluckyCombinationSuccessfulCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Declaring an unlucky combination successful"@en, "Eine ungünstige Wendung für gelungen erklären"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the dice fall badly, accept the result and pronounce it a success."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Coordinating the dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceptingSetbacksToStayOutsideCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting setbacks to stay outside"@en, "Rückschläge annehmen, um draußen zu bleiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Staying outside the mirror requires following the rule of declaring bad combinations successful."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingBeingOutsideTheMirrorCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingDeclaringAnUnluckyCombinationSuccessfulCh19 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Otherwise one remains inside the mirror."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Coordinating the dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDynamicAdjustmentInsteadOfScriptingCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Dynamic adjustment instead of scripting"@en, "Dynamische Anpassung statt Drehbuch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Move the mind's control away from developing scripts to ongoing adjustment, observing the sixth and seventh principles: whenever the mind protests at a deviation from its plan, come to your senses quickly and accept the change as going the way it should; at the start do not worry about means; form the goal image and simply step towards it, treating all that happens as serving the goal; adopt the Maker's intention that all goes as it should because you decided so, neither at the mercy of circumstance nor controlling everything."@en ;
    skos:note "The sixth and seventh principles belong to pmc:TranserfingMirrorPrinciplesCh18."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Coordinating the dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAdjustmentKeepsOneMasterOfTheWorldCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Adjustment keeps one master of the world"@en, "Anpassung hält einen als Herrn der Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "One remains master of one's world while observing the sixth and seventh principles."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDynamicAdjustmentInsteadOfScriptingCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingBeingOutsideTheMirrorCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Coordinating the dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInsistingOnOnesScriptCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Insisting on one's script"@en, "Auf dem eigenen Drehbuch beharren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind pre-plans the course of events, feels failure when events diverge, keeps to the original plan out of clichés and spoils everything; no one can know how events must go, and whoever insists they know gets nothing; stereotypes lock the door to one's dreams."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: the mind pre-plans the course of events, feels failure when events diverge, keeps to the original plan out of clichés and spoils everything; no one can know how events must go, and whoever insists they know gets nothing; stereotypes lock the door to one's dreams; it bears on pmp:TranserfingDynamicAdjustmentInsteadOfScriptingCh19, pmp:TranserfingTargetSlideCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Coordinating the dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRealityTurnsOutPliableCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality turns out pliable"@en, "Die Wirklichkeit erweist sich als formbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: on waking from the mirror daydream one sees oneself amid a vast spherical mirror, part of reality yet separate, as when becoming lucid in a dream; reality responds more slowly than in dreams, but once used to its slower gear one finds it yields to the image in one's thoughts."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingEscapingTheMirrorCh19, pmc:TranserfingBeingOutsideTheMirrorCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'Coordinating the dream'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'
#

pmc:TranserfingThreeGiftsOfTheAlternativesSpaceCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three gifts of the alternatives space"@en, "Drei Gaben des Variantenraums"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beyond the mirror Eternity offers boundless possibilities and three gifts: the future one can materialise, sacred Knowledge that can make one a genius, and a third, the right to one's own verdict."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnPathRevealsTheTreasuresCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Own path reveals the treasures"@en, "Der eigene Weg enthüllt die Schätze"@de ;
    skos:definition "The chosen differ not by reading or talent but by walking their own unique path, where goals and doors are theirs alone; following others repeats their experience. Suspecting this is not integrated awareness, which alone can guide action; the author tells how as a child he found a huge mushroom only after leaving his parents' trail, and how he kept relapsing into the herd afterwards."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAccessToKnowledgeFromEternityCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Access to Knowledge from Eternity"@en, "Zugang zu Wissen aus der Ewigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Drawing ideas, discoveries and works (books, pictures, melodies, even programs and devices) from the alternatives space, where all discoveries and masterpieces already exist; Knowledge not found in any book, said to make one a genius."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGenius: the access is described as drawing finished works out of Eternity, among them programs and devices, by tuning in through the heart."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingElementaryFoundationOfKnowledgeCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Elementary foundation of knowledge in a field"@en, "Elementare Wissensgrundlage in einem Gebiet"@de ;
    skos:definition "A grounding in the basics of the area one is interested in, said to let one attune to the matching sector of the alternatives space; once its first stages are absorbed, what was taught may be forgotten."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part as the prior step the passes linked to knowledge assimilated in action."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingElementaryFoundationBeforeTuningInCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Elementary foundation before tuning in"@en, "Grundlagenwissen vor dem Einstimmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To access information in the alternatives space one must first lay basic knowledge of the field; once the initial stages are absorbed one may forget the teaching."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingDrawingKnowledgeFromSoulInsteadBooksCh15: the basic grounding is stated as a condition with its consequence, and once the first stages are absorbed the teaching may be forgotten."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingAccessToKnowledgeFromEternityCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingElementaryFoundationOfKnowledgeCh19 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without it one cannot tune in to the relevant region of the alternatives space."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHookingIntoASectorCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Hooking into a sector"@en, "Sich in einen Sektor einhaken"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the basics, stop studying the old: hook into the sector with a seed (two or three key chords for a melody, a mood for a picture, a situation for a book); invent nothing, calm the presumptuous mind, let characters find their own way out of the scene and follow the flow, carrying the task methodically from start to finish; take the idea as the starting point and let the flow complete the rest."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOverPlanningComplicatesCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Over-planning complicates"@en, "Überplanung verkompliziert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Planning everything ahead makes the mind build elaborate constructs; the author grants that some projects do need a plan, then follow the flow at least in parts."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingHookingIntoASectorCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHookingYieldsWorksFromTheFlowCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Hooking yields works from the flow"@en, "Einhaken ergibt Werke aus dem Strom"@de ;
    skos:definition "The plot is said to emerge by itself and the flow to supply the most elegant solution."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingHookingIntoASectorCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAccessToKnowledgeFromEternityCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingRecognisingIdeasByHeedingTheHeartCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognising ideas by heeding the heart"@en, "Ideen erkennen, indem man auf das Herz hört"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not invent ideas; leave the crowd, walk your own path following the heart, and recognise the idea when it arrives, since the heart reaches the alternatives space and the mind only interprets."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnPathYieldsIdeasCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Own path yields ideas"@en, "Eigener Weg ergibt Ideen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ideas are said to come via the soul for certain to those on their own path."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingRecognisingIdeasByHeedingTheHeartCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAccessToKnowledgeFromEternityCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAskingAndForgettingTheQuestionCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Asking and forgetting the question"@en, "Die Frage stellen und vergessen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Formulate a question clearly, then forget it for a while; if no answer comes within a few days, ask again from time to time; requires resolve to break stereotypes and the pendulum rule and to stop seeking answers in others' books, shifting intention from receiving to creating."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:TranserfingDrawingKnowledgeFromSoulInsteadBooksCh15: the question is to be forgotten after it is put and asked again from time to time; an answer is promised within days or months."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAnswerWithinDaysOrMonthsCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Answer within days or months"@en, "Antwort binnen Tagen oder Monaten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced: the answer comes within a few days, or over the following months, but it is said to come for sure."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: announced for pmp:TranserfingAskingAndForgettingTheQuestionCh19, pmc:TranserfingAccessToKnowledgeFromEternityCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAssertingTheRightToChooseOneselfCh19 a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Asserting the right to choose oneself"@en, "Das Recht beanspruchen, sich selbst zu erwählen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Claim your right by birth, not merit: declare that from now on you have chosen yourself; establish your own canons; when opinions clash, decide your own truth because your reality has you as its Maker; state your verdict as being capable and worthy because you decided so, intending rather than wanting or hoping."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAssertingTheRightYieldsMakerStatusCh19 a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Asserting the right yields Maker status"@en, "Beanspruchen ergibt den Schöpferstatus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The verdict that one has the right is said to be the ticket to Eternity and licence to be Maker of one's reality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAssertingTheRightToChooseOneselfCh19 ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRightOfTheMakerCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMakerCh19 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Maker"@en, "Der Schöpfer"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Maker is held to be the person who delivers their own verdicts and creates their own reality, as opposed to one who accepts others' verdicts."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Maker" ;
    pm:nameRole "self-chosen creator of one's own reality" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTemerityToAssertTheRightCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Temerity to assert one's right"@en, "Kühnheit, das eigene Recht zu behaupten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Boldness to claim one's right as Maker without doubt or pangs of conscience; the text calls it the only condition of an effective verdict and the trait the Gatekeeper admits."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part as the prior step the passes linked to unity of heart and mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTemerityBeforeAnEffectiveVerdictCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Temerity before an effective verdict"@en, "Kühnheit vor einem wirksamen Urteil"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sole condition is the boldness to assert the right without doubt."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingRightOfTheMakerCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingTemerityToAssertTheRightCh19 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "With doubt or pangs of conscience the verdict loses force and the lawmaker becomes the accused."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheMakersWillMustNotBecomeTheMindsDictateCh19 a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The Maker's will must not become the mind's dictate"@en, "Der Wille des Schöpfers darf kein Diktat des Verstandes werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asserting the right must not turn into the mind dictating against the heart; the verdict must also harm no one."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingAssertingTheRightToChooseOneselfCh19 ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartAndMindOneBeforeTheVerdictWorksCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart and mind one before the verdict works"@en, "Herz und Verstand eins, damit das Urteil wirkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The verdict has power only when heart and mind are one; the explanation must become true knowledge through acting and being convinced by experience."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingRightOfTheMakerCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingEdinstvoDushiIRazuma ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Whoever ignores the heart is not making but making mistakes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingVerdictWithoutTheHeartsAssentCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Verdict without the heart's assent"@en, "Urteil ohne Zustimmung des Herzens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who believe themselves stars while inept (singing without voice or ear) fail because their heart knows they are no good and the mind tries to prove otherwise; such people walk another's path and have not found their real talent."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: those who believe themselves stars while inept (singing without voice or ear) fail because their heart knows they are no good and the mind tries to prove otherwise; such people walk another's path and have not found their real talent; it bears on pmp:TranserfingAssertingTheRightToChooseOneselfCh19."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRightOfTheMakerCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Right of the Maker"@en, "Recht des Schöpfers"@de ;
    skos:definition "The right to deliver one's own verdict on what is true, right and good for one's world and to set one's own canons, called the privilege to be Maker of one's own reality and the third gift of the alternatives space; it brings freedom from oppressive circumstances and quiet confidence, and lets one discard outside judgements, Transurfing's included, provided there is no guilt or indecision and no harm to others. The world is said to agree, as a mirror, with whoever dares a verdict of their own."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAccessToEternityCh19 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Access to Eternity"@en, "Zugang zur Ewigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Entry to everything the alternatives space holds; whatever one wishes with heart and mind is said to be one's own."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGatekeeperCh19 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Gatekeeper"@en, "Der Torwächter"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Gatekeeper is held to be an absolute law at the threshold of Eternity that guards everything there and admits only those bold enough to claim the Maker's right; one's verdict is the entry pass."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Gatekeeper" ;
    pm:nameRole "absolute law guarding access to Eternity" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBoldnessBeforeTheGatekeeperCh19 a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Boldness before the Gatekeeper"@en, "Kühnheit vor dem Torwächter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Access to Eternity is granted only to those who boldly assert their right as Maker."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingAccessToEternityCh19 ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingTemerityToAssertTheRightCh19 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The Gatekeeper denies access to all others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), ch. XIX The Gatekeeper to Eternity, section 'The Maker's Verdict'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .


#
# afterword A Strange Reality
#

pmc:TranserfingPrinciplesInvariantToTheModelAft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Principles invariant to the model"@en, "Prinzipien unabhängig vom Modell"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whatever model underlies Transurfing, its principles stay valid; the alternatives model is a benchmark and aid to grasp principles, not a detailed account of the world; it could be made continuous (dropping life lines) without changing the essence; whether the principles work the reader must find out."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingThoughtEnergyActsDirectlyOnRealityAft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Thought energy acts directly on reality"@en, "Gedankenenergie wirkt direkt auf die Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Key principle: thought energy influences physical reality not only indirectly via action but directly as transmitted physical energy; the author grants science has not accepted this since tests are ambiguous, but holds one cannot wait for its approval."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingSignsOfOuterIntentionGoUnnoticedAft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs of outer intention go unnoticed"@en, "Zeichen äußerer Absicht bleiben unbemerkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author reports that half an hour after weighing whether to cite Jung's beetle, a similar beetle flew through his window and he let it out absent-mindedly, recognising the sign only later; he infers that people live in waking sleep and miss the manifestations of outer intention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingSynchronicityReadAsOuterIntentionAft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Synchronicity read as outer intention"@en, "Synchronizität als äußere Absicht gelesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Carl Jung, the Swiss psychiatrist, gathered acausal coincidences of thought and matter and called them synchronicity; his cases (a day of repeated fish motifs, the rose-chafer beetle arriving as a patient told of a golden scarab) are read here as outer intention at work. In Transurfing's view visualisation sometimes raises a strong gust of it, and both of Jung's readings, thought shaping events or foreseeing them, are accepted: the heart reads the information field, the mind interprets and forms thoughts that, given unity of heart and mind, materialise."@en ;
    skos:note "Jung quotations (On Synchronicity; Synchronicity: An Acausal Connecting Principle, 1960) are interpreted by the author."@en ;
    skos:note "Carl Jung is cited as an investigator, not a named being of the tradition; his quotations are interpreted by the author."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstSpecialRelativitysSpeedLimitAft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Outer intention outside the speed limit of special relativity"@en, "Äußere Absicht jenseits der Lichtgeschwindigkeitsgrenze der speziellen Relativität"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author holds that outer intention, like the instantaneous link of all particles in John Bell's theorem as he renders it, does not conform to special relativity's speed limit, and suggests information exchange may involve no energy at all and so outrun light; he adds that quantum physics too rests on unproven postulates, so no model deserves undue weight."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute in which only the author's side is read; held as a concept, not as pm:Disputing. John Bell is named only as the source of the theorem the author renders, not as a named being."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingObliqueLifeLinesAndTimeShiftsAft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Oblique life lines and time shifts"@en, "Schräge Lebenslinien und Zeitsprünge"@de ;
    skos:definition "Life lines normally run parallel to the time axis; if two were oblique, a transition between them would shift one into past or future, or across space instantly, the slope setting the size and direction; the grandfather paradox dissolves because one is born into another line; the past cannot change, time is static, and only realisation moves over the alternatives like a torch beam over trees."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingStaticTime: oblique life lines are introduced to explain shifts in time and space, and the grandfather paradox is dissolved by birth into another line."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingUFOMotionAsRealisationAtDifferentPointsAft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "UFO motion as realisation at different points"@en, "UFO-Bewegung als Verwirklichung an verschiedenen Punkten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Abrupt UFO accelerations and right-angle turns are explained not as flight but as the object being realised at successive points in the alternatives space, so occupants feel no stress."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingOwnModelOfMemoryMayBeWrongAft a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Own model of memory may be wrong"@en, "Eigenes Gedächtnismodell kann falsch sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author concedes that his earlier argument that the mind cannot store all information, built on a bytes model, may not fit how the brain actually stores information."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingPrinciplesInvariantToTheModelAft ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstMechanisticMaterialistScienceAft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against mechanistic materialist science"@en, "Gegen mechanistisch-materialistische Wissenschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author disputes the materialist tradition that matter comes first and fixes consciousness: studying the brain this way is like a pre-television scientist concluding the set generates its programmes; science and religion as pendulums win dominance by persecuting dissidents, fighting for adherents rather than truth; man is not destined to know everything."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute in which only the author's side is read; held as a concept, not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingUnexplainedKnowledgeIsRejectedByTheMindAft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unexplained knowledge is rejected by the mind"@en, "Unerklärtes Wissen weist der Verstand ab"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind negates whatever lacks a sensible explanation and will not integrate knowledge into its worldview template until convinced of its rationality; hence the mind needs an explanation for Transurfing to be applied."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: the mind negates whatever lacks a sensible explanation and will not integrate knowledge into its worldview template until convinced of its rationality; hence the mind needs an explanation for Transurfing to be applied."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingOnlyPracticalResultsDecideBetweenModelsAft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Only practical results decide between models"@en, "Nur praktische Ergebnisse entscheiden zwischen Modellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Overlap with similar teachings is natural since every teaching is an autonomous model built by people with similar worldviews; asking which describes the world better is pointless, as with branches of mathematics solving one physics problem; only practical results matter, and one must choose."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingOneModelAmongMany: the overlap with similar teachings is explained by similar worldviews, with branches of mathematics solving one physics problem as the comparison."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .


#
# afterword A Strange Reality, section 'The Intention of the Ancient Magicians'
#

pmc:TranserfingTheAncientMagiciansAft a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The ancient magicians"@en, "Die alten Magier"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ancient magicians are held to be keepers of Knowledge in the civilisation before ours, whose fragments survive in scattered esoteric teachings; information, not yet proven, suggests some moved into another reality and now try to hand their Knowledge on to humanity through transcendental channels."@en ;
    skos:note "The author adds that over recent decades people in many places have independently given similar readings of the same Knowledge."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "ancient magicians" ;
    pm:nameRole "Knowledge keepers of a prior civilisation, possibly transmitting from another reality" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality, section 'The Intention of the Ancient Magicians'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingTheGuardianAft a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Guardian"@en, "Der Hüter"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Guardian is the figure the author met in a dream (described in the first chapter); he cannot say for certain he exists, at any rate in our reality, but has much reason to think so; the meeting overturned his worldview and life, the Guardian never reappeared, yet the author sometimes feels his presence."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGuardianOfTheReserve: the author says he cannot be sure whether the Guardian is real, at any rate in our world, though he has reason to think so; the Guardian never came back, yet his presence is sometimes felt."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Guardian" ;
    pm:nameRole "dream figure who initiated the author's Transurfing Knowledge" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality, section 'The Intention of the Ancient Magicians'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingTransurfingAsReceivedKnowledgeAft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transurfing as Knowledge tuned in, not invented"@en, "Transerfing als eingestimmtes, nicht erfundenes Wissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author says he never regarded Transurfing as his own Knowledge or merit but as something he could not have made up, he being only a repeater tuned into the relevant area of the alternatives space after the dream meeting with the Guardian; only putting it into words and systematising it was his own hard labour."@en ;
    skos:note "Not a pm:Receiving: the content is said to be tuned in, not the wording received from another speaker."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:TranserfingGuardianReceiving: the author does not claim another speaker's wording here: he calls himself a repeater tuned into the alternatives space and says the expression and systematisation were his own hard work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality, section 'The Intention of the Ancient Magicians'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingAwarenessAndAdeptnessNotKnowledgeAft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The book yields awareness and adeptness, not Knowledge"@en, "Das Buch gibt Gewahrsein und Geschick, nicht Wissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author tells the reader that devouring the book in one go brings not Knowledge as such but awareness and adeptness, which he insists are different things; the Knowledge is to be assimilated, not only learned."@en ;
    skos:note "Added by the reader of the whole part: missed by both passes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (2006), afterword A Strange Reality, section 'The Intention of the Ancient Magicians'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers; the afterword is not in the Bulgarian translation of this Stupen' (Ябълките падат в небето), which closes instead with a short address На гости на вечността, so whether it belongs to the single volume of 2006 is open" .

pmc:TranserfingTransurfingIsNotATechniqueAft a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Transurfing is not a technique"@en, "Transurfing ist keine Technik"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever seeks step-by-step tricks like instructions for tying a tie will search in vain; creating one's fate does not boil down to a sequence of moves; the point is awareness of inner freedom."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingAwarenessOfInnerFreedomAndMasteryOfTheLayerAft ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen5 ;
